    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/lmu-at-a-glance/awards/excellence-strategy/university-of-excellence/attractive-career-paths/": {
      "title": "Postdoc phase",
      "description": "Attractive career paths - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU LMU at a glance Awards Excellence Strategy University of Excellence You are here: Attractive career paths Attractive career paths for junior academics LMU places a special emphasis on the comprehensive and individual promotion of its junior academics – from undergraduate studies to a professorship. Skip to content Scientific training at an early stage LMU Academic Career Program Doctoral phase Postdoc phase Tenure Track phase Show more Scientific training at an early stage For LMU, high-quality academic teaching consists primarily in imparting scientifically sound judgment on the basis of excellent research. Thus, in order to draw students' interest to research at an early stage and lay the foundations for an academic career, LMU pursues the concept of research-oriented teaching at all stages of academic training. LMU Academic Career Program Using its LMU Academic Career Program, LMU has been successful for more than ten years in creating excellent research and training conditions for outstanding junior academics at all stages of their academic careers – from the doctoral phase to a professorship. LMU uses its funding as University of Excellence to further develop the Academic Career Program, with a particular focus on the career development of postdoctoral researchers. For the individual support of career development, an additional funding line in the Junior Researcher Fund has been introduced and the new Knowledge Transfer Fund has been established. At faculty level , the Postdoc Support Fund provides funding to LMU’s faculties to promote recruitment of international postdocs, to facilitate the continuation of scientific activity for postdocs, e.g. following periods of parental leave or care for relatives (re-entry funding), and to support postdocs’ networking as well as open-access publishing activities. With these funding measures, LMU continues to support junior academics in developing competitive research profiles, with an additional focus on the compatibility of career and family as well as on specific funding needs across individual subject cultures. At the same time, the measures are designed to open up additional networking opportunities and career paths to junior academics, both within and outside of academia. Doctoral phase Graduate Center der LMU The GraduateCenter is the central coordination, advice and service unit for doctoral studies at LMU. Its Doctoral Research Training program offers funding for events for doctoral candidates. During the final phase of their doctorate, doctoral candidates may also apply for Completion Grants. Postdoc phase Junior Researcher Fund The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. Postdoc Support Fund The Postdoc Support Fund provides additional resources to LMU’s individual faculties in order to facilitate flexible, subject-specific promotion of postdoctoral researchers, particularly for the recruitment of international postdocs, for international mobility and networking activities, for promoting the resumption of research activities and promoting the continued pursuit of an academic career following periods of parental leave or care for relatives (re-entry funding), as well as for open-access publishing activities. Junior Researchers in Residence The Junior Researchers in Residence program of the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) offers members of academic staff as well fellows of LMU an opportunity to spend one semester at CAS. Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) Young Center The Young Center of the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) gathers together outstanding LMU junior academics. These include holders of prestigious research funding awards and fellowships (e.g. ERC Starting Grants or DFG Heisenberg Fellowships) as well as LMU Research Fellows . Knowledge Transfer Fund The Knowledge Transfer Fund provides seed funding for projects aimed at the further development of basic research into technological, social or economic innovations. LMUMentoring The LMUMentoring program offers excellent junior academics an opportunity to receive career advice from mentors individually chosen as \"role models\" by themselves as well as to benefit from subject-specific support measures. LMU Research Fellowships The LMU Research Fellowships are directed at outstanding postdoctoral researchers from all fields of research. Since 2017, the Program has been supported by the European Commission’s Marie Skłodowska-Curie COFUND Action. Tenure Track phase Seed Funding The Investment Fund provides seed funding for the procurement of large-scale third-party funding projects directed at innovative research ideas and the establishment of new research fields. The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. LMU Tenure Track Model More than fifteen years ago, LMU was one of the first universities in Germany to implement a Tenure Track Model , offering a predictable career path to a permanent professorship. The success of LMU’s model has been confirmed, for instance, by additional funding for twenty tenure-track professorships awarded to the University as part of the Joint Federal Government-Länder Programme for Junior Academics (WISNA). Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) Young Center The Young Center of the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) gathers together outstanding LMU junior academics. These include holders of prestigious research funding awards and fellowships (e.g. ERC Starting Grants or DFG Heisenberg Fellowships) as well as LMU Research Fellows. Adele Hartman Program The Adele Hartman Program provides additional support for appointments of women to W2 professorships. Career services Academic Careers Graduate Center LMU Research services LMU Gateway Center for Leadership and People Management up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/lmu-at-a-glance/awards/excellence-strategy/university-of-excellence/attractive-career-paths/lmu-research-fellowships/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "LMU Research Fellowships - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU LMU at a glance Awards Excellence Strategy University of Excellence Attractive career paths You are here: LMU Research Fellowships LMU Research Fellowships The LMU Research Fellowships are directed at outstanding postdoctoral researchers from all fields of research. Since 2017, the Program has been supported by the European Commission’s Marie Skłodowska-Curie COFUND Action. Supported by an LMU professor, fellows carry out their own two-year research project and thus sharpen their academic profile. Mobility and networking with international partner institutions are particularly promoted through research stays or collaborations. In addition to Incoming Fellowships for outstanding international early-career researchers. LMU also awards Outgoing Fellowships for excellent postdoctoral researchers who have completed their doctorates in the last twelve months or are about to do so. The LMU Research Fellows are members of the Young Center of the LMU Center for Advanced Studies . Since the start of the LMU Research Fellowship Program in 2009, a total of 74 excellent junior academics have been funded in eight calls, 46 of whom came from institutions abroad, 45 percent were women. Almost all former fellows remained in academia and subsequently obtained attractive positions at renowned academic institutions, including professorships at institutions such as the University of Oxford, New York University, and EPF Lausanne. No further calls are planned at this time. Selected success stories News Getting to Grips with Clouds Read more Meteorologist Linda Forster is an Outgoing LMU Research Fellow engaged on a project on cloud formation at the California Institute of Technology (Caltech) and at LMU Munich. The results may help predict future climate change. News Travel broadens the mind Read more Chemist Henry Schurkus is the first Outgoing LMU Fellow. As part of his Fellowship, he worked at the California Institute of Technology in Pasadena. His project could help to make hydrogen production more carbon-neutral. News Object lessons Read more Art historian Philippe Cordez extracts hidden connotations from objects preserved from pre-modern times. He joined LMU as a Research Fellow and subsequently headed a Junior Research Group funded by the Elite Network of Bavaria. Contact Patricia Frohberg Research Strategy Unit Coordinator LMU Research Fellowships Send an email +49 89 2180-3702 More This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation Programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Grant Agreement No. 754388. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/international-network/lmu-stellenbosch-university-su-research-cooperation-program/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU International network You are here: LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program LMU-Stellenbosch University (SU) Research Cooperation Program The LMU-SU Research Cooperation Program was established in 2025 to promote and support research collaboration between LMU Munich and Stellenbosch University (SU). Enlarge The LMU-SU partnership is open to all disciplines and supports joint research and partnership development projects, workshops, conferences, as well as mobility opportunities for early-career researchers and professors. Call for Applications For the 2027 funding period , researchers from LMU and Stellenbosch University are invited to submit joint applications for funding within the LMU–SU Research Cooperation Program. Funding is available for joint research activities, including research projects, workshops and conferences, as well as individual mobility. Applications may request funding of up to €25,000 for the funding period from January 1 to December 31, 2027 . Eligible applicants are researchers holding a doctoral degree who are employed at LMU or Stellenbosch University. Doctoral candidates are not eligible to apply as Principal Investigators (PIs) but are expressly encouraged to participate in the projects. The application process for the 2027 funding period is expected to open in September 2026. Further information on the call and application process will be published on this website in the coming weeks. LMU–SU Networking Week An LMU–SU Networking Week is held annually as part of the funded research projects. The event brings together funded researchers from different disciplines and is hosted alternately by LMU and Stellenbosch University. It aims to promote interdisciplinary and international exchange , strengthen connections among the funded projects, and generate new ideas and opportunities for further collaboration. Impressions from the LMU–SU Networking Week 2026 are available in the video. 28 Aug 2026 Information on Further Funding Opportunities In addition to funding available through the LMU–SU Research Cooperation Program , researchers may consider BayIntAn – Promoting Cooperation , a funding program of the Bavarian Research Alliance (BayFOR) that supports the development of international research collaborations. Within the framework of this initial funding for international research cooperation, eligible travel expenses of up to €10,000 may be reimbursed. Further information on the funding conditions and application process is available on the Bavarian Research Alliance website . For further information or questions, please contact the LMU International Office at network.international@lmu.de or the academic coordinator, Prof. Dr. Alexandra Kertz-Welzel. Academic Coordinators Universität Stellenbosch: Prof. Herman Wasserman LMU München: Prof. Dr. Alexandra Kertz-Welzel Contact Program Coordination Stellenbosch University: Sarah van der Westhuizen via sarahvdw@sun.ac.za LMU Munich: Hannah Weckemann via network.international@lmu.de up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/international-network/lmu-csc-scholarship-program/open-doctoral-positions/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Open doctoral positions - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU International network LMU-CSC Scholarship Program You are here: Open doctoral positions LMU - CSC Program: Open doctoral positions Some of our researchers and/or institutes define research projects especially for the Joint LMU - CSC Program. These open positions are very specific. Please apply for one of these positions ONLY if it conforms with your research interests and qualifications. New open positions for 2027 will be published in October 2026. Find all information on the LMU - CSC Scholarship Program. Read more Browse through our list and select the open position that best reflects your interests and skill set. Contact the International Office, referring explicitly to the position that interests you. Contact the researcher/institute concerned directly and also cc the CSC coordinator at LMU's International Office Ms Dongmei Zhang . Please note: If you are interested in a subject area not covered by the list of open positions, you can contact the respective faculty and find a supervisor on your own. Here are further details on how to find a supervisor at LMU . Open positions offered by the Faculty of Medicine Details regarding new open positions offered by the Faculty of Medicine can be found on the faculty's website. Open positions offered by the Graduate School Life Science Munich (LSM) New open positions offered by the Graduate School of Life Science Munich (LSM) up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related