    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/working-at-lmu/academic-careers/qualification-and-personal-development/tenure-track-phase/": {
      "title": "Qualification and personal development for the tenure track phase",
      "description": "Tenure track phase - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Qualification and personal development You are here: Tenure track phase Qualification and personal development for the tenure track phase Our comprehensive qualification program enables you to continuously improve in the competence fields “subject knowledge and methodology”, “didactics, communication and cooperation”, “leadership and management”, as well as “self-competence and career planning”. Boost your career potential! Skip to content September December Further qualification offers Contact September Date Time Event title Host 21 September 2026 9 a.m. PROFiL Basisseminar - für Neuberufene (in German) PROFiL 21 September 2026 9 a.m. PrüfenPlus-Qualifizierung (in German) PROFiL 22 September 2026 9 a.m. ERC Starting and Consolidator Grant Workshop (restricted access) Research Funding 24 September 2026 9 a.m. Alumni und Alumnae als Lernpartner:innen – Praxiswissen lebendig in der Lehre nutzen (in German) PROFiL December Date Time Event title Host 10 December 2026 10 a.m. First audition? Applying for (junior) professorships ( Registration opens on 29 October 2026 ) Research Funding Further qualification offers Intercultural training and workshops (LMU Gateway) IT courses and trainings (restricted access) Teaching support services (eUniversity - restricted access) Certificate for Teaching in Higher Education of the Bavarian Universities (PROFiL) Career mentoring for female junior academics (LMU EXTRA) Realistic appointment-training for female junior academics (University Women's Representative) LMUMentoring Seminar for research-based entrepreneurship (LMU Spin-off Service - restricted access) Seminar series \"Transfer Skills\" (Transfer and Entrepreneurship - restricted access) Qualification opportunities at LMU Klinikum (University Hospital) AHA Academy Professional development for LMU employees Subject-specific opportunities for further qualification can be found on the websites of our faculties , research projects , and doctoral programs . Note for international junior academics: Please be aware that some of our events are currently only available in German. We are constantly updating and improving what we have on offer. Please do feel free to contact us if you have any questions! Contact Research Services Elisabethplatz 22 80796 München Directions (https://maps.app.goo.gl/sawNuPPZZvr2tYUh8) researchservices@lmu.de Send an email +40 89 2180-72280 up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/working-at-lmu/academic-careers/funding-opportunities/": {
      "title": "The postdoc phase",
      "description": "Funding opportunities - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers You are here: Funding opportunities Funding opportunities at LMU Shape your career by getting the right help from the start! LMU offers perfect research and career development conditions, spanning all phases of your academic journey — from doctorate to professorship. The LMU Academic Career Program provides outstanding junior researchers with ideal research and qualification conditions. At every career stage - from doctorate to postdoc to tenure track and finally to lifetime professorship - LMU offers a wide range of interdisciplinary and subject-specific funding opportunities and services to support you in developing your scientific independence and a competitive research profile, in networking both within and outside academia, and in balancing career and family. Funding opportunities for the career phase you're in Change content The doctoral phase The postdoc phase The tenure-track phase The doctoral phase During your doctoral phase, LMU is here to champion your academic qualification, professional development and career planning. Information on support services for doctoral candidates is provided by the LMU Graduate Center — the central coordination, advisory and service facility for doctoral studies at LMU . Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . The postdoc phase Whether you're on the road to a professorship or pursuing a career outside of academia, LMU supports you in your postdoctoral phase to get your career well planned out. We do this by helping you broaden your international horizons and establish yourself as an independent researcher through networking and mobility. Research: The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. Through the Junior Researchers in Residence program, the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) offers outstanding junior academics an attractive opportunity to conduct intensive research on a single topic for one full semester. The CAS Young Center comprises outstanding LMU junior academics, including holders of renowned awards and scholarships. The Postdoc Support Fund provides additional resources to LMU’s individual faculties to facilitate flexible, subject-specific promotion of postdoctoral researchers, particularly for the recruitment of international postdocs, to facilitate the continuation of scientific activity, e.g. following periods of parental leave (re-entry funding), for networking activities, as well as for open-access publishing activities. Some faculties present their Postdoc Support Fund offers on dedicated websites: Faculty of Catholic Theology Faculty of Protestant Theology Faculty of Economics (integrated in the Junior Development Program) Faculty of Medicine Faculty of History and the Arts: History Department Faculty of History and the Arts: School of the Arts Faculty of Philosophy, Philosophy of Science and Religious Studies Faculty of Languages and Literatures (integrated in the Nachwuchsförderprogramm) Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Mathematics, Informatics and Statistics Faculty of Geosciences (integrated in funding@geo) The Knowledge Transfer Fund provides seed funding for projects aimed at the development of basic research into technological, social or economic innovations. Internationalization: Through the Postdoc Support Fund , established as part of the LMU's funding as a University of Excellence, our faculties promote international networking , from conference trips to hosting your own conferences and workshops. Some faculties present their Postdoc Support Fund offers on dedicated websites (see above under „Research“). Harnessing LMU's international network, postdocs are given a number of opportunities to build international networks and take advantage of mobility. This is enabled, for example, via the many strategic partnerships nurtured by LMUexcellent or the Erasmus+ mobility network. Mentoring: Within the scope of the LMU Mentoring program, excellent junior academics can seek career advice from personally selected mentors and receive subject-specific guidance in developing their careers. Publication: The LMU Open Access Fund supports open access publications with a grant towards publication costs. Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . The tenure-track phase The Tenure Track Model offers junior academics an early-stage, attractive career path towards a permanent professorship at LMU. Tenure-track professors at LMU can draw on a variety of support in building their academic profile. Research: The Investment Fund provides seed funding for the procurement of large-scale third-party funding projects directed at innovative research ideas and the establishment of new research fields. The Junior Researcher Fund promotes the individual career development of junior academics (who have gained no more than six years of professional academic experience since having completed their doctorate) by providing support for the independent procurement of externally funded and peer-reviewed research projects, particularly of prestigious research prizes and awards directed at junior academics. As a forum for cross-disciplinary academic exchange, the Center for Advanced Studies (CAS) promotes various types of cooperative research and academic exchange. The CAS Young Center comprises outstanding LMU junior academics, including holders of renowned awards and scholarships. Internationalization: By harnessing LMU's international network, there are numerous opportunities to build international networks and take advantage of mobility . This is enabled, for example, via the many strategic partnerships nurtured by LMUexcellent or the Erasmus+ mobility network. Equal opportunities: In order to increase the proportion of women among professors, the Adele  Hartmann Program additionally promotes the appointment of outstanding female researchers to W2 professorships. Publication: The LMU Open Access Fund supports open access publications with a grant towards publication costs. Subject-specific funding opportunities can be found on the sites of our faculties , collaborative research projects , and doctoral programs . Further funding opportunities Funding and support services of the University Women's Representative Funding opportunities by the Munich University Association (in German) Advice on third-party funding programs We are here to share information and advise you when it comes to the requirements and success factors for third-party funded research projects. Research services Information events on funding programs (restricted access) Funding database Pivot-RP (restricted access) At a glance The right support for the postdoc phase (PDF, 96 KB) The right support for the tenure-track phase (PDF, 124 KB) up Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/working-at-lmu/academic-careers/funding-opportunities/stibet-mentoring-scholarship-program/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Funding opportunities You are here: STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program for international doctoral candidates The STIBET Mentoring Scholarship Program offered by the German Academic Exchange Service (DAAD) supports particularly qualified foreign doctoral candidates. The DAAD has currently suspended the program \"STIBET Doktoranden”. Therefore, no scholarships can be awarded. Further information will be provided here on this webpage as soon as the program is re-opened. Aim Thanks to these resources we can individually support extraordinarily qualified international doctoral students. The aim is to integrate excellent international doctoral candidates into the international activities of their respective department. Scholarship type and objective The International Office awards scholarships for particularly committed doctoral candidates. The aim of these scholarships is to improve support for foreign students and doctoral candidates by having scholarship students take on support tasks or perform other services conducive to international exchange within their faculty. Prerequisites The main prerequisite for funding is the commitment of the scholarship student to promoting the department and support in the supervision of international students, e.g. through social and professional mentoring, language tandems, cooperation in cultural programs, field trips, local interest events, support activities in student housing, and language courses, among others. The decisive criterion for a successful application is a candidate's outstanding academic performance. Applicants who receive funding from the DAAD under another program are not eligible to apply. Application procedure Please fill out the application form (PDF, 99 KB) . In addition, a current resume and two letters of recommendation from your supervising professors must be included. Please email all materials by 15 December to Dr. Dongmei Zhang International Office CSC programs Send an email +49 89 2180-6169 More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/about-lmu/working-at-lmu/academic-careers/career-options/moments-of-choice/": {
      "title": "The postdoc",
      "description": "Moments of choice - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home About LMU Working at LMU Academic Careers Career options You are here: Moments of choice Moments of choice An academic education offers you a wide range of career opportunities. In this video series, nine people report on their personal careers and provide insights into significant moments for their individual career decisions. Let them inspire you! Skip to content The postdoc The professor The returnee from industry The entrepreneur The science manager The employee in the cultural sector The employee in industry The employees in the media sector Contact Show more The video series titled “Moments of Choice – Academic Career Paths” introduces you to people who have an academic degree from LMU and/or work at LMU. In each video, we show an individual portrait for a possible career. Whether a postdoc, professor, returnee from industry, science manager, founder, or person who has chosen a career outside of academia, our videos provide exciting insights into individual career paths and personal motivations for choosing a specific career. Particularly valuable are the tips that our testimonials would like to pass on to junior scientists in decision-making situations. LMU aims for comprehensive support Are you at a crucial point in your career? Would you like to get an overview of your options or reflect on an upcoming career decision? Speak with us. Our career counselling (restricted access) offers you professional support tailored to your personal needs so you can make the best decision and achieve your career goals. The postdoc If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 03:26\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t11 Jan 2023\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU The professor If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 05:09\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t18 Jan 2023\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU The returnee from industry If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 03:09\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t25 Jan 2023\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU The entrepreneur If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU da