    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/job-portal/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Job portal - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Job portal Job portal & Career Network Get the practical experience you need to complement your studies and launch an exciting career. Here, students can find internships in Germany and abroad, working student positions, part-time jobs and positions for direct entry after graduation. You can also enjoy exclusive job opportunities through companies that are members of our career network. Job portal for LMU's students & doctoral candidates You are an employer and want to become part of the network: Click here to see what we offer employers . You will also find our prices and terms and conditions for the job portal for employers there. LMU Career Services excellent Network To our partner companies – LMU Career Network . Students at LMU have particularly good opportunities at our approximately 100 partner companies. Please refer to our Career Service and Career Events in your application. This will significantly increase your chances of being accepted. Team Job-Portal LMU's Career Services Office / Job portal Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/job-portal/manual/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Manual - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Job portal You are here: Manual LMU Career Services: Manual Job portal Here you will find a quick guide to the job portal. After logging in, you can also request individual support at any time by clicking on the corresponding button. Registration Enlarge Employers can use this page to register and post jobs. If you are a premium partner of the LMU Career Service, please contact us. We will then enable you to post ads free of charge. Login Enlarge If you have successfully registered, you can log in using this mask field. So that you do not have to enter the identifier and e-mail used again and again, you will receive a short link when you log in, which pre-fills the two fields. Please save this as a favorite. Main Menu Enlarge In the main menu you will find all the functions for the job exchange: Home : Click here to return to the home page My Details : Please enter your personal and billing data for your company here. Enter the standard address here. You have the option of entering a different billing address for each advertisement. Create / Admin Job Ad s: Here you can post a new job advertisement and/or change previously published ones for the remainder of the term. You also get an overview of your users (user overview) and sub-accounts (customer list). You can also create sub-accounts and invite other users by e-mail. Invoices : Here you will find an overview of your invoices and which of them may still be outstanding. Accounts : If you wish, you can use our offer for premium partners and create a separate account in the Career Service Portal. You only need to remember the login details for the job portal. You can use accounts to switch between the job exchange and the Career Service Portal at any time. Support : You can use this button to give us access to your account at any time (for seven days). We will be happy to help you with your problem directly. Post Job Ads 1 Enlarge Create new customer/sub-account : For example, if you are a recruitment agency managing several clients/customers, you can create sub-accounts for them here. Client list : Here you can see an overview of your customers/sub-accounts. User list : Here you can see an overview of users who can post jobs alongside you. (see also Create additional users) Job details : Use this tab to enter all information about the respective job. Employer details : Use this tab to enter general information about your company/client, including your logo. Add another user : Here you can invite colleagues by e-mail address so that they can also post jobs. Create new job ad : This is where you create a new job advertisement. Post Job Ads 2 Enlarge Your already published job ads : In the drop-down menu you will find any job advertisements you already have. \"new\" stands for advertisements that have not been fully processed and therefore not published Job title (m/f/x) : Enter a descriptive title for your job here. Ad link and/or PDF : You can either provide a link to the job (recommended). Or you can upload a PDF (max. 3MB). Or do both. Optional: Your reference : Here you can enter further information for your accounting department. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/career-talk/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career Talk - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: Career Talk LMU Career Talk 2026 The LMU Career Talk is the annual highlight for all those who want to actively shape their professional future. Every year we focus on a new, highly topical career topic that will shape the working world of tomorrow. LMU Career Talk on July 10, 2026 Enlarge High school graduation, college, dream job! — Everything's going according to plan... right? Look forward to an inspiring panel discussion in the morning, where renowned experts from various industries will share exciting insights and practical tips on the latest career trends. Let the experiences and stories of successful professionals motivate you and discover new perspectives for your own career. Moderator: Lothar Wüst - Managing Director, Cormens Anne Brier – Director of the Mentoring Program at the Munich Press Club / Journalist for Bayerischer Rundfunk, among others Dr. Markus Gruber – Director General, Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs Pascal Heß – Labor Market Economist at the IAB (Institute for Employment Research) Eva Kraatz – Coach and Trainer—including for the LMU mentors / long-time mentor Elke Pfnür – HVB Unicredit Germany – Archivist & Historian at the Bank Alexander Vocelka - Senior AI Advisor - ThinkaDo Following that, and in preparation for the networking lunch buffet: World Café on the Topic: Career Instead of Knockout in the Age of AI Moderator: Dr. Stephan Pflaum The afternoon is all about networking : Here, students from all disciplines have a unique opportunity to make valuable connections and exchange ideas across industries. Take this chance to learn from your fellow students’ experiences, make new friends, and expand your professional network. The LMU Career Talk is more than just an event—it’s your springboard to a successful future. Join us and take an active role in shaping your career! Participating companies: ADAC Basycon Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs FTAPI Goethe-Institut HypoVereinsbank - UniCredit Germany IAB - Institute for Employment Research innoscripta City of Munich, IT Department SwissRe Press Club SIXT ThinkaDo The event will take place at the Kardinal-Wendel-Haus in Munich. Schedule Time Program item starting at 8:30 a.m. Check-In 9:00 a.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Opening Remarks: Dr. Markus Gruber, Director General of the Bavarian State Ministry of Family, Labor, and Social Affairs Opening Remarks: Dr. Margit Weber, Vice President for Equal Opportunity, Talent Development, and Diversity 9:15 a.m. – 11:45 a.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Panel discussion with renowned experts (see above) . Followed by a World Café on the topic \" Career Instead of Knockout in the Age of AI\" 12:00 p.m. – 1:30 p.m. Lunch & Networking Area (near the Great Hall and in the palace gardens) Networking Lunch 12:30 p.m. – 4:00 p.m. Main Hall, Ground Floor Smart Job Fair & Keynotes Resume Reviews at the FTAPI Booth 1:00 p.m. – 2:30 p.m. Library, 1st Floor Keynote: AI in Your Career! Have the Courage to Use It! - Viola Kraus ( Pre-registration required ) 2:30 p.m. – 5:30 p.m. Library, 1st Floor Workshop: Have the Courage to Pursue a Career! Have the Courage to Make Decisions! - Anne Brier ( Pre-registration required ) 2:00 p.m. – 6:00 p.m. Conference Room, 1st Floor Workshop: AI & Career @ Career Talk, Beginner-Friendly Workshop with the LRZ ( Pre-registration required ) around 4:15 p.m. End of the event Impressions 2025 & 2024 Previous Next Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Dirk Erfurth LMU's Career Services Head of Career Service / Business Coach Advanced Send an email More Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/career-marathon/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career Marathon - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: Career Marathon LMU Career Marathon - Diversity & Career In parallel to the company presentations, there will be exciting presentations on the topics of diversity, integration and careers. Renowned speakers will report first-hand on the importance of these topics in their companies and how they are put into practice on a daily basis. LMU Career Marathon on October 23, 2026 Enlarge The Career Marathon is the event for anyone who wants to find out all about their career options. Here, students have the opportunity to get to know up to 20 companies from a wide range of industries and make valuable contacts. Gender equality in careers Queer Career Inclusive career opportunities Learn firsthand how diverse the working world really is and how companies benefit from integration and diversity. Be inspired and discover new career prospects that will help you shape your individual career path. Use the Career Marathon as a springboard for your professional future. Join us and experience a day full of new impressions, valuable encounters, and innovative ideas! Event language: German / English Registration Location: Cardinal Wendel House . Participating Companies and Organizations ADAC CIL Strategy Consultants d-fine Erzdiözese München Futrue Iskander Business Partner KPMG McDonald's Mediaschool Bayern Medpace PwC START Munich SwissRe TEG The Entrepreneurial Group UniCredit List is updated constantly. Timeline Hop-on-hop-off concept: You decide when to join and leave the event. 10:00 a.m. Event Start 11:00 a.m. – 11:45 a.m. Keynote I Topic tbd 12:00 p.m. – 1:00 p.m. Networking Lunch for Students and Companies 1:00 p.m. – 1:45 p.m. Key Note II Topic tbd 2:00 p.m. – 6:00 p.m. \"Diversity & Career\" Workshop 4:00 p.m. End of the Career Fair Previous Next Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
