    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/workshops-and-seminars/seminars-for-acquiring-soft-skills-and-application-relevant-knowledge/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Seminars for acquiring soft skills and application-relevant knowledge Seminar series \"Endlich Montag!\" | Dates 2026 Skip to content August 2026 September 2026 October 2026 November 2026 December 2026 Show more August 2026 31.08.2026 Mindful Interactions: Menschenkenntnis als Schlüsselkompetenz für den Berufseinstieg (online, DE) 31.08.2026 | 9 am - 1 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: german| Trainer: Raoul Sonnenberg Sign up! Wir alle haben uns im Laufe des Lebens in vielen Situationen kennengelernt und haben intuitive Eindrücke von anderen. Doch oft fehlt uns eine klare Systematik, diese Eindrücke weiter zu vertiefen und etwas Greifbares daraus zu machen. Motiv-Typologien helfen uns dabei, zügig ein deutliches Bild zu Stärken und Interessen bei uns selbst und anderen zu gewinnen und dieses Wissen auch tatsächlich in der Kommunikation und Beziehungsgestaltung einzusetzen. Unsere Kommunikation wird deutlich authentischer, kraftvoller, sensibler und überzeugender und in Auseinandersetzungen entstehen Lösungen, die wirklich tragfähig sind. Inhalte: Motiv-Typologie: Charakteristische Haltungen & Verhalten verstehen Analyse-Fähigkeit: Stärken & Interessen bei uns selbst und anderen im Alltag erkennen Überzeugungskraft: die entscheidenden Hebel in der Kommunikation nutzen Konfliktlösung: die Motive hinter Einwänden und Kritik erkennen und auf Lösungen ausrichten September 2026 07.09.2026 Successful use of Artificial Intelligence in the Job Application Process (online, EN) 07.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sing up! Artificial Intelligence is rapidly transforming how we search for jobs, prepare applications, and present ourselves to employers. At the same time, organizations are increasingly using AI-stools in recruiting and selection. But what does this mean for you, entering the job market? In this interactive 4-hour online workshop, you will gain a practical overview of the role of AI in today's job application process and learn about current developments. Together, we will explore how to use AI effectively and responsibly when preparing applications, CVs, cover letters, and interview preparations. The workshop combines expert input with hands-on exercises, reflection, and peer exchange. You will actively work on examples, discuss trends, and get time to individually work on your AI driven recruiting strategy and documents. By the end of the workshop, you will: Understand how AI is changing recruitment and hiring practices. Learn how AI can support different stages of your application process. Gain practical tips and develop ideas for preparing your future career in a changing world of work. 14.09.2026 Gesprächs-Führung – Gespräche kraftvoll und zielgerichtet führen (online, DE) - cancelled 14.09.2026 | 9 am - 1 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: german | Trainer: Raoul Sonnenberg Gespräche und Meetings nehmen eine zentrale Stellung in unserer Zusammenarbeit ein. Wir tauschen wichtige Informationen mit Partnern aus, erarbeiten passende Lösungen und führen Entscheidungen herbei. Allerdings bleiben Einzel- & Gruppengespräche oft hinter den Möglichkeiten zurück: Themen fransen schnell aus, die Zeit läuft aus dem Ruder, die Ergebnisse sind angesichts der insgesamt eingesetzten Zeit oft mittelprächtig. Für Verantwortliche macht das manchmal wenig Freude und ist besonders bitter, wenn es um wichtige Themen geht und viel Herzblut in den Projekten steckt. Wie können wir über unsere Gesprächs-Führung den Austausch so gestalten, dass das Gespräch von Anfang an gelöst und produktiv läuft und sich alle zielorientiert beteiligen? Und wie können wir durch eine effektive Steuerung das Gespräch (selbst bei Hindernissen und Störungen) aufmerksam auf Kurs halten und zu klaren, verbindlichen Ergebnissen führen? Inhalte: Gespräche zielorientiert einleiten Gespräch auch bei Störungen kraftvoll auf Kurs halten Negative Beiträge auf den konstruktiven Weg zurückführen Die Verbindlichkeit von Ergebnissen sichern 14.09.2026 LinkedIn for Career Starters: How to land a job with the right profile (online, EN) 14.09.2026 | 2 - 4 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Julia Barden Sign up! Would you like to create a convincing LinkedIn profile that leaves a positive impression on potential employers? Are you unsure how to present your qualifications convincingly? Would you like to actively use your LinkedIn profile for your job search? The workshop is highly practical. After every short theory input, you will have time to work directly on your own LinkedIn profile while receiving examples, guidance and practical tips. By the end of the workshop, you will have a professional, (almost) complete LinkedIn profile that is ready to support your job search, as well as a clear understanding of how to use it effectively. In this online workshop you will learn: How to create a professional LinkedIn profile from scratch What to write in each important profile section, including your headline, About section, experience, education and skills How recruiters search for candidates and how to optimize your profile to appear in search results How to use keywords strategically How to use LinkedIn effectively for job searching and networking 21.09.2026 Strategic and effective Jobsearch (online, EN) 21.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Carolin Martin Sign up! Gain fundermantal insights into the hiring process (AI aspects included) while learning how to build a compelling personal brand and defining your ideal career profile. Develop your application strategy, prepare your documents accordingly and discover practical interview techniques to help you stand out with confidence. Having lead the Recruting team at Apple Retail in Germany for more than 10 years our trainer will share all her knowledge, actionalbe tools and a clear plan for your successful jobsearch. 28.09.2026 Salary negotiations: How to handle the tricky question with confidence (online, EN) 28.09.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Salary discussions can be challenging - but with the right preparation, they become an opportunity. In this two-hour online seminar, participants explore salary and benefits models, understand what influences pay, prepare for interviews and compensation talks, and gain valuable insights into the EU Pay Transparency Directive. October 2026 05.10.2026 Projektmanagement für den Berufseinstieg - effizient & resilient (on site, DE) 05.10.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: german | Trainer: Angela Firmhofer Sign up! In diesem Workshop lernen Sie wesentliche Aspekte und Werkzeuge des Projektmanagements kennen und nutzen, um für den späteren Berufseinstieg bereits zentrale Elemente des Projektmanagements ausüben zu können. Sie lernen eigene Projekte zu entwickeln, zu planen, zu managen und bei unerwarteten Herausforderungen im Projektverlauf handlungsfähig zu sein. Außerdem bekommen Sie Tipps, was bei der Kommunikation im Projektteam und über ein Projekt zu beachten ist. Inhalte Projekte und deren Kreisläufe verstehen Projekte mithilfe von Kreativitätstechniken und Canvas entwickeln und ausarbeiten Projektziele, Arbeitspakete und Meilensteine definieren und terminieren Planen und priorisieren von einzelnen Projekten, Arbeitspaketen und -schritten im Alltag Kommunikation für das Projekt: intern (Team) und extern (Stakeholder*innen) 12.10.2026 Legal framework for working in Germany: Rights & obligations, employment contract, salaries, references (online, EN) (online, EN) 12.10.2026 | 2 - 5 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language : english | Trainer: Violaine Storp Sign up! Seminar Topics: Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labour law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salarly is calculated and what is is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code 19.10.2026 Assessment Center Training (on site, DE) 19.10.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: german | Trainer: Eric Fritzsche Sign up! In diesem Workshop lernen Sie alles, was Sie über das „Assessment Center“ wissen müssen. Außerdem werden Sie mit praktischen Übungen gut darauf vorbereitet. Historie, Hintergrund und Ziele des Assessment Centers Die wichtigsten Übungen im Überblick Vorteile und Nachteile für beide Seiten Zielgerichtete Vorbereitung auf das Assessment Center Analyse und Einsatz der Soft Skills Selbstpräsentation Stärken und Schwächen positiv darstellen Techniken eines erfolgreichen Selbstmarketings Umgang mit kritischen Fragen Beobachter- bzw. Bewertungsbögen Wirkung und Körpersprache Dos and Don‘ts im AC 26.10.2026 Young Leadership Skills – First Steps into Leadership/Supervision (on site, EN) 26.10.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sign up! Leadership or supervision skills are essential in many careers, in different stages of your life. Whether you are planning a career in business, science, public service, or academia, the ability to lead yourself and others is a critical skill. This interactive 4-hour online workshop offers a practical introduction to the foundations of effective leadership/supervision. Together, we will explore key topics that young professionals encounter when taking responsibility for projects, teams, or initiatives: Core responsibilities and expectations of a leadership role + common leadership styles The fundamentals of communication How to navigate difficult conversations Giving and receiving constructive feedback Understanding your own expectations, values, and leadership mindset Through practical examples, reflection exercises, and interactive discussions, you will gain valuable insights into what successful leadership looks like and how you can begin developing your own leadership style. We suggest to take the www.16personalities.com prior to our workshop to gain some initial insights and then come and join our interactive session. November 2026 02.11.2026 Making career & professional decisions (on site, EN) 02.11.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Eva Kraatz Sign up! What will I do after college? Which job and which professional environment are the best fit for me? What exactly do I want? There are so many possibilities—which one is right for me? Deciding which career path to pursue after graduation isn’t always easy. In this seminar, we’ll explore our personal values, among other things, because they play a crucial role in shaping our lives—even if we’re often unaware of it. When we understand our values, we can make career decisions that are not only a good fit but also sustainable. The afternoon will be rounded out with various tips and tricks for general decision-making. In this workshop, we’ll cover the following topics: Hierarchy of personal values Tips and tricks for decision-making and more 09.11.2026 Konfliktmanagement für deinen Berufseinstieg (on site, DE) 09.11.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: german | Trainer: Eva Kraatz Sign up! Konflikte begegnen uns überall im täglichen Leben: in der Familie, im Freundeskreis, in der Uni, im Sportverein, im Job.... Konflikte sind überall vorhanden aber notwendig und meist lösbar. In diesem Workshop beschäftigen wir uns mit: verschiedenen Arten von Konflikten Kommunikation im Konflikt innere Haltung Lösungsmöglichkeiten 16.11.2026 Application Workshop for Internationals (on site, EN) 16.11.2026 | 10 am - 4 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be difficult. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more important things for finding your job in Germany. 23.11.2026  Präsentationsskills & Kommunikation (on site, DE) 23.11.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel Sign up! 30.11.2026 Navigating Germany: Building Intercultural Competences to Connect, Collaborate, and Thrive (online, EN) 30.11.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Angela Kraft-Chan Sign up! Living and studying in Germany involves navigating more than just academic life. It means understanding unwritten rules: how feedback is handled, how trust is built with others, or how group dynamics work in projects, all of which feel different than back home. Thriving in an international career takes more than expertise, but also interpersonal skills to act across cultures. In this interactive workshop, you’ll learn to decode intercultural dynamics and develop practical skills to connect, communicate, and collaborate with greater confidence. Together, we'll explore: Key cultural dimensions such as communication, trust-building, or risk management styles, and how they show up in situations you already recognise How cultural differences can lead to misunderstandings, and what you can do about it Practical communication tools and phrases you can use right away You'll leave with: A clearer framework for understanding cultural differences Develop your own authentic communication style with hands on tools navigating intercultural moments More confidence to express and show up as your authentic self Who is this for? Internationals who want to feel more at ease and more effective in German social and professional settings; and locals who want to thrive in an increasingly intercultural environment. December 2026 07.12.2026 Die Macht der Fragen – Gespräche führen, Menschen aktivieren, Lösungen finden (online, DE) 07.12.2026 | 9 am - 1 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: german | Trainer: Raoul Sonnenberg Sign up! Ob im Studium, im ersten Job, im Bewerbungsgespräch, in Prüfungssituationen oder im Austausch mit Professor, Wissenschaftler und Kolleg:innen: Wer gute Fragen stellt, wirkt klarer, souveräner und professioneller. Fragen helfen, Situationen schneller zu verstehen, Unsicherheiten zu klären, Gesprächspartner einzubeziehen und gemeinsam zu tragfähigen Lösungen zu kommen. Gute Gespräche scheitern selten daran, dass Menschen zu wenig wissen – sondern häufig daran, dass zu schnell bewertet, argumentiert oder aneinander vorbeigeredet wird. Gerade in anspruchsvollen Gesprächssituationen ist es entscheidend, nicht nur die eigene Meinung gut zu vertreten, sondern auch die richtigen Fragen zu stellen: Was ist wirklich gemeint? Worum geht es im Kern? Welche Interessen, Erwartungen oder Bedenken stehen dahinter? Was braucht es, damit ein nächster sinnvoller Schritt möglich wird? In diesem halbtägigen Online-Seminar lernt Ihr, wie Ihr mit Fragen Gespräche öffnen, strukturieren und wirksam steuern könnt. Ihr erfahrt, wie Ihr Gesprächspartner aktiviert, Informationen gezielter gewinnt, Missverständnisse vermeidet und vom Problemreden ins konstruktive Denken führt. Inhalte Fragearten gezielt einsetzen: Gespräche öffnen, echtes Verstehen ermöglichen und Gesprächspartner aktivieren Klarheit gewinnen: Kernthemen, Interessen, Erwartungen und Motive schneller erkennen Gespräche steuern: mit Steuerungsfragen fokussieren, strukturieren und den roten Faden behalten Souverän reagieren: auch bei Unsicherheit, Druck oder komplexen Gesprächssituationen handlungsfähig bleiben Lösungsorientiert fragen: vom Problemreden zum konstruktiven Denken und zu konkreten nächsten Schritten führen Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/workshops-and-seminars/knowledge-relevant-to-job-applications-and-careers/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Knowledge relevant to job applications and careers Seminars relevant to job applications and careers Skip to content 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? 14.10. Career decisions made easy 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch 28.10. Preparation for job interviews, telephone and online interviews 18.11. Business Knigge 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students 02.12. Assessment center: The supreme discipline among selection procedures 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references 16.12. LinkedIn workshop \"How To Use LinkedIn\" Show more 09.09. Future of Work - AI and Career Anmeldung Read more 09.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - online (Zoom) - max 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Viola Kraus \"Future of Work - How the topic of (generative) AI will challenge us now and in the future and how we can learn to deal with it in order to make use of it\" Everyone is talking about AI, generative AI (GenAI). Companies want to use it in a targeted manner and some of us are asking ourselves \"what do I need to know, what else should I learn\". As an active member of our society, as future employees and teachers, we can prepare ourselves for these complex questions and the unknown. What should we already know and what can we still learn? Which gadgets can be used where and how, and are they used by companies? What unknowns are we likely to have to deal with? And what contribution can each of us make to society? 23.09. How do I present myself at a job interview? Anmeldung Read more 23.09.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Englisch - Trainerin: Eva Kraatz In this workshop you will get a good understanding of how to prepare for a job interview. The following topics will be covered: General preparation for your job interview: Company and market environment About me (skills, questions, expectations, how I fit in with the company, etc.) Basic information on interview situations and more 14.10. Career decisions made easy Anmeldung Read more 14.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Eva Kraatz What do I do after university? Which job, which professional environment suits me best? What exactly do I want? There are so many options, which one is right for me? It is not always easy to decide which career path to take after graduation. In this seminar, we will look at our personal values, among other things, as these have a decisive influence on our lives - albeit often unconsciously. If we know our values, we can not only make suitable but also sustainable professional or career decisions. The afternoon will be rounded off with various tips and tricks for general decision-making. In this workshop we will work on the following topics: Personal values Hierarchy of personal values Tips & tricks for decision-making ...and even more... 21.10. Strategic and effective Jobsearch Anmeldung Read more 21.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Englisch - Trainerin: Heike Anne Dietzel - Karrierecoach Searching for a new job can be a very time-consuming and long effort: there are hundreds of job search engines, matching portals and companies post their vacancies on Social media. What is the most effective way to find a new job? Get a glimpse behind the scenes of the recruiting process Build your application strategy that matches your background, personality and interests Understand the variety and evaluate job search channels for your needs Do’s and Dont’s for your communication with Hiring Managers and Recruiters during your job search Define effective networking channels for job search 28.10. Preparation for job interviews, telephone and online interviews Anmeldung Read more 28.10.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career coach A job interview can be conducted in very different ways and is always a major challenge. That's why preparation is a central key to being successful in a job interview. Personnel selection: What criteria are used to evaluate an applicant? Different types of job interviews How can I score points as an applicant in a job interview? Self-presentation as an important key to success in an interview Personal branding: positive self-marketing techniques How do I convince people in a conversation and what role does my body language play? Classic, provocative questions and inadmissible questions The most important do's and don'ts for telephone and online interviews 18.11. Business Knigge Anmeldung Read more 18.11.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Deutsch - Trainer: Isabelle Krier / Eric Fritzsche Immer da, wo Menschen aufeinander treffen gibt es Regeln für den Umgangs miteinander. Manche davon werden offen ausgesprochen, andere sind „ungeschriebene Gesetze“. Auf jeden Fall wird das neue Umfeld ungewohnt sein. Je mehr jedoch darüber bekannt ist, desto selbstsicherer wird dein Auftreten als Berufsanfänger:in sein. Das gilt für ein Praktikum, den Werkstudenten-Job oder die erste „richtige“ Stelle. In diesem Workshop lernst du ein paar einfache Regeln, wir erkunden gemeinsam den Weg durch den „Business Dschungel“ und wir verhelfen dir zu einem gesunden Maß an Selbstsicherheit für einen guten Start. Inhalte: Was sind die typischen Fettnäpfchen? Gibt es (noch) eine Kleiderordnung? Einfluss der Unternehmenskultur auf das Miteinander Der Alltag im Büroleben/Home-Office/Business-Meetings, worauf muss ich achten? Umgang mit Social Media – während und nach der Arbeit Firmenfeiern Geschäftsessen und vieles mehr 25.11. Application Workshop for International Students Anmeldung Read more 25.11.2024 - 10:00 - 16:00 - live&local - Hansa Haus München (Saal) - max. 20 participants - language: English - Trainer: Janine Müller Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be irritating. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more good to know things for finding your job in Germany. 02.12. Assessment center: The supreme discipline among selection procedures Anmeldung Read more 02.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - IBZ Munich - max. 20 participants - Language: German - Trainer: Eric Fritzsche In this seminar we prepare you for assessment centers in a practical way. 09.12. Rights and obligations at work in Germany: employment contract, salaries, references Anmeldung Read more 09.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 - Hansa Haus Munich (Läugerzimmer)- max. 20 participants - Language: English - Trainer: Heike Anne Dietzel - Career Coach Receiving a work contract is an exciting moment as it represents the last step to becoming a part of a company. Signing the contract will be legally binding and the contracts contains the most critical elements of your employeeship. Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labor law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salary is calculated and what is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code 16.12. LinkedIn workshop \"How To Use LinkedIn\" Anmeldung Read more [abgesagt] 16.12.2024 - 16:00 - 20:00 Uhr - Hansa Haus München (Läugerzimmer) - max 20 TN - Sprache: Deutsch - Trainerin: Susanne Kößler Der Workshop richtet sich an alle Studierenden, die durch gezieltes und praxisnahes Training ein erfolgreiches berufliches Netzwerk über LinkedIn auf- oder ausbauen wollen. Anhand wertvoller Praxisbeispiele tauchen wir in die Welt des Netzwerkes ein. Sie erhalten praktische Hilfestellungen, wie Sie Ihr Profil am besten nutzen können und welche Möglichkeiten Sie damit haben. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
