    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/workshops-and-seminars/microsoft-certificate-ai-it-security/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events Workshops and Seminars You are here: Microsoft Certificate AI & IT-Security AI&I Are you interested in artificial intelligence and want to understand how AI can influence your studies and professional life? In our practice-oriented seminar you will learn what AI agents really are, how to develop them, and how to use them effectively. For students of all faculties! AI & I Dates 2026 Registration Read more September 25, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with JetBrains - AI & Code with PyCharm & Co : Registration October 16, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Microsoft : Empowered by AI - Career and Skill Development. Xheneta Krasniqi Registration October 23, 2026 - AI IT / AI Case Workshop with EY Parthenon : Registration Oct. 30, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with Ecodynamics Masterclass 2 (online) Registration November 6, 2026 - AI Case Workshop with the Artificial Intelligence Center Hamburg (ARIC) - Maria Tcharnetsky: AI & Ethics: What to Look Out For, and Do We Need a New Ethical Compass? Registration 11/20/26 - AI Case Workshop with GEMA Registration Nov. 27, 2026 AI Case Workshop with LMU - Dr. Stephan Pflaum: From the Perfect Prompt to a Personal Agent. (online) Registration 12/04/26 - AI Case Workshop with AUDI/LMU : Business vs. Academia Registration 12/11/26 AI Case Workshop with THINKaDo - Alexander Vocelka: AI Governance for a Prosperous Future - How to Co-Exist Registration Over the next few weeks, we will schedule the topics across the various dates. Each module will be available for individual registration. Artificial intelligence has long been a part of our everyday lives—but do you know how it works and how you can use it yourself? In this interactive seminar series, you’ll gain a practical, easy-to-understand, and well-founded introduction to the world of AI agents. Whether you plan to work in research, business, media, government, or NGOs in the future, a basic understanding of AI and its applications is becoming increasingly important. We are offering this seminar series in cooperation with: Microsoft Ecodynamics EY Parthenon GEMA LMU AI Hub Leibniz Computing Center SAP What to Expect: The AI Academy offers both beginners and advanced learners a wealth of practical content on the application of AI in various learning, teaching, work, and everyday settings. All seminars are designed to be hands-on. In addition to the opportunities, we also highlight the risks associated with this new technology, which has become indispensable. The overall focus: how to use AI correctly and effectively in various fields. Target audience: Students from all disciplines in the humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, linguistics, and business—no prior knowledge required! Join us and learn how to use AI effectively in your studies and career. This project is also currently being turned into a book: The AI Compass for Students: How to Use AI Effectively in Your Studies and Career. (Expected to be published by Springer Gabler in 2026) Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Anfrage Workshop up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
