    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/lmu-karriereforum/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "LMU Karriereforum - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: LMU Karriereforum LMU Karriereforum 2026 Cross-industry career fair for students and doctoral candidates from all disciplines and at all stages of their studies. Walk-ins are welcome. The event is open to students and doctoral candidates from all universities and colleges. LMU Career Forum on May 22, 2026 Enlarge Your stepping stone into the professional world Discover your career opportunities at the LMU Career Fair! The Career Fair offers you the opportunity to connect with up to 30 leading companies from a wide range of industries. Take advantage of this chance to meet potential employers, build valuable professional connections, and get a behind-the-scenes look at exciting companies. What can you expect? Direct interaction: Meet HR managers and company representatives in person. Information booths: Get information on internships, part-time student jobs, trainee programs, and career entry opportunities. Keynote Speeches: Attend engaging keynote speeches that offer valuable insights and tips for your career planning. Networking: Connect with others and expand your professional network. Venue: Kardinal Wendel Haus, Munich Time: 10 a.m. – 4 p.m. Participating companies Sign up! Read more Academy Consult ADAC Altman Solon Bank of China Celonis CIL Strategy Consultants Crown Futrue Hubert Burda Media HypoVereinsbank UniCredit KPMG matorix Mediaschool Bavaria Medpace Mercer ProSiebenSat.1 Media SE SwissRe TEG ThirdBridge WiB Women in Business Hop-on, hop-off. We recommend planning at least two hours for the day. The event language is German. Program optional table caption Time Program starting at 9:30 a.m. Check-in, welcome coffee 10:00 a.m. Start of the career fair 12:00 PM – 1:00 PM Networking Lunch 1:00–1:45 p.m. Keynote @ADAC : Working where it really counts. Helping others is our passion. The ADAC as an employer. (Conference Room, 1st Floor) 4:00 p.m. End Impressions LMU Karriereforum 2024 Previous Next Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-and-networking-events/working-here-abroad-your-international-career-in-bavaria/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services Career and networking events You are here: Working here & abroad: your international career in Bavaria LMU International Career Event \"Working here & abroad\" 2026 This event is aimed at international students at LMU and all students who are interested in working in an international environment. Date: November 13, 2026 Registration for workshops recommended. Participation in the career fair (from 12:00 noon) is also possible spontaneously and without pre-registration. Working in an international environment Enlarge Twice a year, we offer this event, which is aimed not only at domestic students but especially at international students. Date for the winter semester: November 13, 2026 Are you a student with an international background looking to establish a long-term career in the German job market? Building personal connections with local companies is a particularly important step in this process! Our event gives you the opportunity to do just that. You’ll meet companies with a presence both in Germany and internationally and discuss your career prospects and entry-level opportunities with them. Representatives from the Bavarian University Centers will also be on hand to offer guidance. Are you a student interested in working in an international environment and looking for the right starting point? This event offers you great opportunities to establish lasting personal connections with international employers from the business, social, and political sectors. The Bavarian University Centers in attendance will provide career counseling (including in academia) within their respective country groups. We recommend that you have German language skills at the B2 level. Sign up! for the event Read more The fair will be accompanied by workshops on professional networking, job applications, and starting a career. This year, for the first time, there will be an afternoon panel discussion featuring international LMU alumni who have successfully entered the German job market . Under the theme “My Career Journey in Germany,” three international alumni will share their paths to their careers, as well as their experiences, challenges, obstacles, and lessons learned. Afterward, you’ll have the opportunity to ask questions. The discussion will be held in English. Registration is recommended. Zhixin Liu , Consultant in the Technology & Transformation practice @Deloitte Pengyang Gao , Treasury Specialist, Shared Services @Toyota Kreditbank / Toyota Financial Services Germany Ke Zhang , Investment Risk Analyst at Allianz Commercial Venue: Kardinal Wendel Haus, Munich Participating Companies & Organizations Amazon amiga München BAMF (Hotline „Arbeiten und Leben in Deutschland“) BAYHOST - Bayerisches Hochschulzentrum für Mittel-, Ost- und Südosteuropa BTHA - Bayerisch-Tschechische Hochschulagentur BayFrance - Bayerisch-Französisches Hochschulzentrum GEMA Goethe Institut innoscripta LMU International Internships Make it in Germany: das Portal der Bundesregierung für Fachkräfte aus dem Ausland Mediaschool Bayern MUNTUM - Model United Nations (MUN) SwissRe TEG The Entrepreneurial Group ThirdBridge UNICEF UniCredit This list is updated regularly. Schedule Hop-on-hop-off concept: You decide when to join and leave the event. 9:00 a.m. - 10:30 a.m. Workshop I : \"Design Your International Career through Design Thinking\" (Violaine Storp) - Registration 10:30 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. Workshop II : \"Job Applications on the International Job Market\" (Viola Kraus) - Registration 11:30 a.m. - 1:30 p.m. Networking Lunch for Students, Companies, and Organizations 12:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Career Fair , Networking 3:00 p.m. - 4:30 p.m. \"My Career Journey in Germany!\" - Success Stories & Panel Discussion - Registration International LMU alumni share their stories of successful careers in Germany. Impressions 2024 & 2025 Previous Next Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/personal-advice/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Personal advice - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Personal advice Personal advice on careers and career entry We advise LMU students and doctoral candidates on all aspects of careers and career entry. Our advisory services for LMU students and doctoral candidates Career coaching for students and doctoral candidates Sign up If you are enrolled at LMU Munich, you can take advantage of personal and individualized advice offered through our Career Services. Expect a consultation to last about one hour. Possible topics to explore might be: Your career goals Your future prospects post bachelor, master or doctorate degree Your career entry Your job application questions Your employment opportunities For a personal consultation, please register in our portal. Under event participation you will find, among other services, personal career counseling. The interviews take place either online or on-site. Please get in touch with us as early as possible, as we always have a lot of requests and waiting times may sometimes be a little longer than expected. Application coaching for students and doctoral candidates Sign up Get your questions concerning your application answered in an individual Zoom session or a local appointment. Possible topics: Application process Job intervies Application documents (e.g. feedback on application letters) Assessment center CV-Check / Job reference-Check Sign up CV-Check Sign up Job reference-Check We will give you feedback on your CV or job reference. Procedure: Sign up via the LMU Career portal . Upload all relevant documents. Please arrange an appointment with us via our online calendar. We will then contact you... via video conference (Zoom or Skype): Job reference-Check or via email: CV-Check You can also find tips and advice on your application documents here . We ask you to implement the tips before booking a CV-Check. Advice on internships abroad We are currently not offering in-person counseling for internships abroad. If you have any questions, please contact us at praktika.careerservice@lmu.de You can find more information about internships abroad here . Career coaching for LMU alumni Did you study at LMU and have now been working for several years? Have you gained important experience during your professional career, achieved goals, and learned from your mistakes? We offer our graduates individual sessions based on the concepts and methodologies of systemic coaching. In a one-to-one session, we will help you to identify your individual goals, plan next steps, overcome potential barriers and move forward in your personal and professional development. These sessions take place in a safe environment. Confidentiality is guaranteed. Possible topics you may bring to the table include: Decision making Professional (re)orientation Evaluation of personal competences and resources Dealing with current challenges Establishing future prospects in terms of your personal or professional development Target group LMU Munich graduates with a maximum of ten years professional experience gained after graduation. Next steps Please write your coaching topic in a short email to us and we will contact you for an appointment. Pricing / Organization One coaching hour (approx. 60 minutes) costs 120,- Euro. The first hour serves to get to know each other and to answer any unanswered questions about the coaching process and is therefore free of charge. Depending on the topic, a structured coaching process can last up to five hours. The duration of the coaching process and the individual appointments are coordinated between coach and coachee. The meetings take place in a central, quiet location in Munich or via video conference. What coaching is certainly not Coaching is neither a form of training nor a formal professional attainment. Specific proposals for actions to be taken or solutions to problems are not offered by the coach and no typical \"advice\" is given. Coaching is not a substitute for psychological, psychotherapeutic or psychiatric advice or treatment. Please note that we do not coach LMU employees in view of possible conflicting interests. Career counseling for LMU junior academics As you embark on your academic career path, different questions will arise. Let us support you with services to help you define and achieve your career goals.Support for doctoral candidates. Counseling academic careers Support for doctoral candidates Please understand that in certain cases we may not be able to offer our counseling services at all, or only to a limited extent. This applies in particular to potential conflicts of interest , as well as when the nature of a counseling request overlaps with legal counseling, therapeutic counseling, or other protected forms of counseling . If you have previously been employed, are currently employed, or are seeking employment at LMU - for example, as a student or research assistant, as a faculty member, or as a researcher - we therefore reserve the right to refer you to an appropriate external counseling service . This is to ensure independent, professionally appropriate counseling and to protect all parties involved. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/career-mentoring/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Career mentoring - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Career mentoring LMU Career Mentoring program - Your tandem to success Is my dream job just a dream? Will I manage the transition from studying to working? How can I stand out in my job application? Which core qualifications should I have? How do I make career contacts? These are lots of questions. Have you thought about reaching out to someone who is already in the job, industry or company that you'd like to be? Skip to content Greeting from Minister of State Ulrike Scharf (StMAS) The LMU Career Mentoring Programme at a glance Further information on the procedure and registration Insights LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 Introducing a mentoring tandem Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Show more Greeting from Minister of State Ulrike Scharf (StMAS) If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 2:00\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t22 Nov 2024\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©StMAS The LMU Career Mentoring Programme at a glance Registration for mentees & mentors Read more Your mentoring relationship is one of the best opportunities to reflect on your professional and personal plans with an experienced person . Often, your mentor will be your direct guide to your first job. Our approximately 300 volunteer mentors are experienced academics from all disciplines and from a wide variety of industries and professions . They answer your questions, share their experiences and accompany you to help you get your career off to a successful start. Our mentees and mentors agree: mentoring is great fun and helps them advance both professionally and personally. The fact that many former mentees return to us as mentors a few years later speaks for itself. The duration of the mentoring tandems is entirely individual: anything is possible, from a few weeks to several months or even long-term relationships, depending on the needs of the mentees and the capacities of the mentors. How often you meet is also individual: as a rule, mentors and mentees meet in person once or twice every six months and also keep in touch by telephone or email. In the tandem, you can freely discuss all topics related to starting your career, your studies and your career . Topics, times and locations are determined by the mentor and mentee themselves. During various events , such as the golf event or theatre visits, both sides can expand their network to include other mentors and students. Further information on the procedure and registration Information & registration for students Sign up If you are enrolled at LMU – whether as an undergraduate or doctoral student – you can register as a mentee at any time. Your field of study or semester of study are irrelevant. After you register, we will support you in selecting your mentor in a personal consultation. LMU Career Mentoring process: Register as a student at any time via the Career Service Portal . Fill out your personal profile completely. Register for the Career Mentoring Programme via the portal (important: include a brief description of your motivation). Select a date for the ‘mentoring interview’ (Zoom or on-site). After the interview, we will provide you with a selection of suitable mentors. Please select up to two mentors. As soon as the person you have chosen has agreed to the tandem, you will receive a confirmation email from us. Get in touch with your mentor! You and your mentor will design your tandem individually. You will decide together how often you meet, whether in person or virtually, whether you keep in touch beyond that, and what you talk about. Information & registration for mentors Sign up Are you an academic with three or more years of professional experience ? Then we would be delighted to have you join our programme as a volunteer mentor. We welcome LMU alumni and graduates from other universities who have the time and desire to volunteer as mentors to support LMU students in their career choices. We welcome mentors from all industries and professional fields. We offer virtual exchange and networking meetings for our mentors several times a year. In addition, we organise cultural or sporting exchange meetings in and around LMU at regular intervals. Mentors also receive a free copy of our Mentoring Compass book. LMU Career Mentoring procedure: Please register once on the LMU Career Service Portal . Fill out your personal profile in full. Then register for the Career Mentoring Programme via ‘Events & Services’. It is important to provide information about your professional background and your motivation, as this information will be displayed to the students. If you are interested, please register directly for a virtual introductory webinar or further exchange meetings. Late registration is possible at any time. As soon as a student has chosen you as their mentor, we will notify you. You then have the option of accepting or rejecting the pairing via the portal. Once you have agreed, your mentee will contact you shortly. Please be patient – it can sometimes take a few weeks for the first match to be made. We hold weekly selection interviews with students from all departments. If you have any questions, please feel free to contact us at any time by email . You and your mentee will design your tandem individually. You will decide together how often you meet, whether in person or virtually, whether you keep in touch beyond that, and what you talk about. Events for mentors LMU Mentoring-Forum: annual networking and exchange event with keynote speeches on the topic of mentoring (6–9 p.m., Literaturhaus Munich) Thursday, march 5 2026 Sign up! Introductory webinars for new mentors (18:30 - 19:30, Zoom) Tuesday, May 19, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, September 22, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, December 8, 2026 Sign up! Mentoring consultation hours for mentors – questions, exchange, networking (18:30 - 19:30, Zoom) Tuesday, April 14, 2026 Sign up! Tuesday, October 6, 2026 Sign up! Voraussetzung: Vollständige Registrierung als Mentor / Mentorin Insights LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 The LMU Career Mentoring Forum 2026 took place on March 5 at the Literaturhaus München. The program included personal exchanges, networking, and substantive input on the topic of mentoring. Previous Next Introducing a mentoring tandem If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. 19 Jan 2021 Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/offers-for-international-students/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Offers for International Students - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Offers for International Students Career Services for International Students & Doctoral Candidates We support international students & doctoral candidates at LMU with customized services to help them gain a foothold in the German job market. Skip to content Career events and seminars 2026 September 2026 October 2026 November 2026 Business German courses Personal counseling services LMU Career Mentoring Program Additional Sources of Information Your contact Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners Show more Enlarge Are you a student with an international background and want to gain a foothold in the Bavarian or German job market? Whether you are interested in internships, working student positions, part-time jobs or a permanent position in a German-speaking country - we will support you on your career path. We offer international students of the LMU exclusive Career events, Seminars Professional language courses and Personal consulting services On this website you will find an overview of our services. Career events and seminars 2026 You are of course cordially invited to all career events. You can find an overview of all events here . September 2026 07.09.2026 Successful use of Artificial Intelligence in the Job Application Process (online, EN) 07.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sign up! Artificial Intelligence is rapidly transforming how we search for jobs, prepare applications, and present ourselves to employers. At the same time, organizations are increasingly using AI-stools in recruiting and selection. But what does this mean for you, entering the job market? In this interactive 4-hour online workshop, you will gain a practical overview of the role of AI in today's job application process and learn about current developments. Together, we will explore how to use AI effectively and responsibly when preparing applications, CVs, cover letters, and interview preparations. The workshop combines expert input with hands-on exercises, reflection, and peer exchange. You will actively work on examples, discuss trends, and get time to individually work on your AI driven recruiting strategy and documents. By the end of the workshop, you will: Understand how AI is changing recruitment and hiring practices. Learn how AI can support different stages of your application process. Gain practical tips and develop ideas for preparing your future career in a changing world of work. 14.09.2026 LinkedIn for Career Starters: How to land a job with the right profile? (online, EN) 14.09.2026 | 2 - 4 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Julia Barden Sign up! Would you like to create a convincing LinkedIn profile that leaves a positive impression on potential employers? Are you unsure how to present your qualifications convincingly? Would you like to actively use your LinkedIn profile for your job search? The workshop is highly practical. After every short theory input, you will have time to work directly on your own LinkedIn profile while receiving examples, guidance and practical tips. By the end of the workshop, you will have a professional, (almost) complete LinkedIn profile that is ready to support your job search, as well as a clear understanding of how to use it effectively. In this online workshop you will learn: How to create a professional LinkedIn profile from scratch What to write in each important profile section, including your headline, About section, experience, education and skills How recruiters search for candidates and how to optimize your profile to appear in search results How to use keywords strategically How to use LinkedIn effectively for job searching and networking 21.09.2026 Strategic and effective Jobsearch (online, EN) 21.09.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Carolin Martin Sign up! Gain fundermantal insights into the hiring process (AI aspects included) while learning how to build a compelling personal brand and defining your ideal career profile. Develop your application strategy, prepare your documents accordingly and discover practical interview techniques to help you stand out with confidence. Having lead the Recruting team at Apple Retail in Germany for more than 10 years our trainer will share all her knowledge, actionalbe tools and a clear plan for your successful jobsearch. 28.09.2026 Salary negotiations: How to handle the tricky question with confidence (online, EN) 28.09.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Salary discussions can be challenging - but with the right preparation, they become an opportunity. In this two-hour online seminar, participants explore salary and benefits models, understand what influences pay, prepare for interviews and compensation talks, and gain valuable insights into the EU Pay Transparency Directive. October 2026 12.10.2026 Legal framework for working in Germany: Rights and obligations, employment contract, salaries, references (online, EN) 12.10.2026 | 2 - 5 pm | online (Zoom) | 20 participants max | Language: englis h | Trainer: Violaine Storp Sign up! Seminar Topics: Mandatory elements of a work contract under German labour law Types of employment and work contracts Most important rights and obligations of the employee and the employer Working hours and vacation regulations Probation period, termination of the contract and period of notice Final checklist before you sign the contract How your salarly is calculated and what is is composed of Work certificates & references in Germany and how to understand the secret code 26.10.2026 Young Leadership Skills – First Steps into Leadership/ Supervision (on site, EN) 26.10.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Viola Kraus Sign up! Leadership or supervision skills are essential in many careers, in different stages of your life. Whether you are planning a career in business, science, public service, or academia, the ability to lead yourself and others is a critical skill. This interactive 4-hour online workshop offers a practical introduction to the foundations of effective leadership/supervision. Together, we will explore key topics that young professionals encounter when taking responsibility for projects, teams, or initiatives: Core responsibilities and expectations of a leadership role + common leadership styles The fundamentals of communication How to navigate difficult conversations Giving and receiving constructive feedback Understanding your own expectations, values, and leadership mindset Through practical examples, reflection exercises, and interactive discussions, you will gain valuable insights into what successful leadership looks like and how you can begin developing your own leadership style. We suggest to take the www.16personalities.com prior to our workshop to gain some initial insights and then come and join our interactive session. November 2026 02.11.2026 Making career & professional decisions (on site, EN) 02.11.2026 | 2 - 6 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Eva Kraatz Sign up! What will I do after college? Which job and which professional environment are the best fit for me? What exactly do I want? There are so many possibilities—which one is right for me? Deciding which career path to pursue after graduation isn’t always easy. In this seminar, we’ll explore our personal values, among other things, because they play a crucial role in shaping our lives—even if we’re often unaware of it. When we understand our values, we can make career decisions that are not only a good fit but also sustainable. The afternoon will be rounded out with various tips and tricks for general decision-making. In this workshop, we’ll cover the following topics: Hierarchy of personal values Tips and tricks for decision-making and more 16.11.2026 Application Workshop for Internationals (on site, EN) 16.11.2026 | 10 am - 4 pm | Hansa Haus München | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Janine Müller Sign up! Other countries, other manners - applying for your first job in Germany Getting started for your first job in Germany can be difficult. We will give you a good overview about the way to apply for a job in Germany among the candidate lifecycle: How to read job advertisements? What to prepare for the formal application? How can you prepare yourself for the job interview to make a great first impression? What is necessary to know for you first day and the onboarding period? ...and many more important things for finding your job in Germany. 30.11.2026 Navigating Germany: Building Intercultural Competences to Connect, Collaborate, and Thrive (online, EN) 30.11.2026 | 4 - 6 pm | Zoom | 20 participants max | Language: english | Trainer: Angela Kraft-Chan Sign up! Living and studying in Germany involves navigating more than just academic life. It means understanding unwritten rules: how feedback is handled, how trust is built with others, or how group dynamics work in projects, all of which feel different than back home. Thriving in an international career takes more than expertise, but also interpersonal skills to act across cultures. In this interactive workshop, you’ll learn to decode intercultural dynamics and develop practical skills to connect, communicate, and collaborate with greater confidence. Together, we'll explore: Key cultural dimensions such as communication, trust-building, or risk management styles, and how they show up in situations you already recognise How cultural differences can lead to misunderstandings, and what you can do about it Practical communication tools and phrases you can use right away You'll leave with: A clearer framework for understanding cultural differences Develop your own authentic communication style with hands on tools navigating intercultural moments More confidence to express and show up as your authentic self Who is this for? Internationals who want to feel more at ease and more effective in German social and professional settings; and locals who want to thrive in an increasingly intercultural environment. 13.11.2026 LMU International Career Event \"Working here & abroad\" Career & Networking event for international students & doctoral candidates from all faculties. 9:00 - 10:30 a.m. Workshop I : \"Design Your International Career through Design Thinking\" - Sign up! 10:30 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. Workshop II : \"Job Applications on the International Job Market\" - Sign up! 12:00 p.m. - 5:00 p.m Career Fair with up to 20 companies and organizations , Networking - Sing up! 3:00 - 4:30 p.m. \"My Career Journey in Germany!\" - International LMU alumni share their stories of successful careers in Germany. (panel discussion) - Sign up! More information can be found here . Business German courses Online Self-Study Course: “Starting a Career and Working Life in Germany” Online self-study course from Deutsch-Uni Online (DUO) Duration: approx. 100 hours Course level: B1; suitable for students at levels A2–B2 Free for students at LMU Munich. Registration . Tutored Professional Language Course “German for Career Starters” (B2/C1) Dates: New dates will be announced here In cooperation with Deutsch-Uni Online (DUO) This is an online course. The content is partly offered in a flexible self-study format , and you will also receive support from a tutor : 8 virtual group meetings (thursdays from 6:30 pm, 70 minutes each) 3 individual feedback sessions on submitted work 4 moderated topics in the forum Certificate of completion upon active participation Required language proficiency: B2 Time commitment: approx. 50 total learning hours Deposit: €75 (we will refund the deposit after the course ends if you have successfully completed at least 75% of the course) Topics: Well-prepared for the job interview Successful communication with colleagues Handling large amounts of information Project work Grammar topics: Causal structures, adjective declension, relative clauses, participial attributes, nominal and verbal style Please note that only students and doctoral candidates enrolled at LMU are eligible to take the course. Please upload your enrollment certificate via the portal. Personal counseling services Infos & Anmeldung Read more Take advantage of our wide range of personalized consulting services: Resume Check: The formal and content requirements vary depending on the country where you're applying. Let us review your resume or cover letter and receive valuable tips and advice via email. Job Reference Review: Have you received a job reference in a German-speaking country and would like feedback on it? Get that feedback during a brief, one-on-one conversation. Personal Career Counseling: Do you have questions about your prospects after graduation, your opportunities, or how to start your career? Get personalized, one-on-one advice on any questions you have about starting your career. Job Application Counseling: Do you have specific questions about your current job application? Ask us during a one-on-one consultation. You can find important information about German-language application materials here. Walk-in office hours* on Thursdays from 11 a.m. to 12 p.m. Address: Ludwigstraße 27, Room G211 No appointment necessary. We will notify you here if an office hour is canceled. *The open office hours are not a substitute for individual career or job application counseling and are intended solely as a first point of contact for general questions. Please note that time is limited. LMU Career Mentoring Program Enlarge Your mentoring relationship is one of the best opportunities to reflect on your professional and personal goals with an experienced person. Mentors often serve as direct guides to your first job. Our approximately 300 volunteer mentors are experienced professionals with college degrees in a wide range of fields, representing a diverse array of industries and occupations. The LMU Career Mentoring Program offers you the following benefits: You'll be assigned a personal contact - an experienced professional - who will be there to assist you with your questions and concerns. This will give you direct insights into your target industry, application processes, and the German job market. You'll have the opportunity to participate in a wide variety of events, allowing you to expand your personal and professional network in Germany. Information & Registration Additional Sources of Information We recommend that you achieve at least a B2 level of German proficiency before applying for jobs in German-speaking countries, as this is a requirement for many companies. Here you will find the general German courses offered at LMU. Volunteering can be a great way to meet people, practice German, and gain your first practical experience. You can find an overview of LMU student clubs and initiatives here . LMU International Student Guide LMU Gateway for International Doctoral Candidates Social Services and Scholarship Counseling for International Candidates Conflict Resolution and Anti-Discrimination Make it in Germany - the official website for qualified professionals The German government’s official multilingual portal , “Make it in Germany,” provides reliable information on all aspects of living and working in Germany. The website offers qualified professionals and international students all the relevant information on visas and residence permits, as well as on career prospects after completing their studies in Germany. Amiga Munich Your contact Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dieses Projekt wird aus Mitteln des Bayerischen Staatsministeriums für Familie, Arbeit und Soziales gefördert. Funding partners up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/ambassador-program/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Ambassador Program - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Ambassador Program Peer-to-peer Ambassador Program Our new cohort of ambassadors will start in the winter semester 2024/25. The next introductory seminar will take place on 25.10.2024. To the application Become a student ambassador in the LMU Career Community! Link to registration Read more Our career network of students from all departments and companies, as well as mentors from all industries and professions, should continue to grow and enable you to successfully start your career. As one of 10 ambassadors per semester, you will help us inform students about our offerings and expand our reach. We will train you in an exclusive seminar to become a successful networker. You will receive a certificate from us about your commitment and training. Special attention is given to reaching our international students. So if you are an international student yourself, you are especially welcome to join our program! Your Ambassador Responsibilities: You support the LMU Career Community in growing. You make your fellow students aware of our community in lectures and seminars. In social networks such as Instagram or LinkedIn, you share our posts (with content suitable for you and your fellow students). You forward our information about events, seminars or consulting offers (that match your study / interest profile) to your friends. You will help us with the supervision of our trade fair stand. You help us establish a lasting connection with your faculty. You will be actively involved in our social media presence. If you are interested, you can also get involved in the implementation of our career events. Your advantages: In your first semester as an ambassador, we will train you to be a successful networker in an exclusive seminar . You will get insights \"behind the scenes\" of the Career Service and make a variety of contacts. You will always be up-to-date regarding our events and offers and will be partially involved in the planning. You will receive exclusive LMU Ambassador business cards. You will receive a certificate for your voluntary commitment as an ambassador. Your profile: You are at least in your second semester (Bachelor or Master). You are interested in career topics and active networking and share our information reliably and appropriately with your fellow students. You have already participated in some of our events. You are willing to actively support us as an ambassador for at least one semester. Ambassadors from all faculties of the LMU are welcome. To become an ambassador, please apply via our portal . Your contact More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/internships-abroad/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Internships abroad - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Internships abroad Internships abroad Overcome borders - open up perspectives. An internship abroad enhances your professional development, improves your chances of securing a job and broadens your horizons. Gain international business experience Further information about your stay abroad Read more An internship abroad is a valuable addition to your academic education and strengthens your individual profile for the job market. Our services include: Guidance on planning your internship abroad Preparation and funding support for your stay Insights from internship experiences around the world You can find our information brochure for internships abroad here (PDF, 1,448 KB) . More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/cultural-sporting-events/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Cultural & sporting events - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Cultural & sporting events Career Community: Cultural & sporting events At our cultural and sporting events we invite you to hang out in a relaxed environment and meet our LMU corporate partners, mentors, alumni, as well as other students. Cultural events Join us at the theater, an art show or music event. As a member of our Career Community you'll be invited to enjoy buzzing networking buffets, receive tickets for VIP seats and backstage passes and hook up with trending artists and art directors. Members of our Career Community won't need to spend a single dime. Holz oder Eisen? Karriere heißt Entscheidungen treffen (in German) Registration form Read more Please find mor information on our German Event-Site . German listening skills B2 are recommended to attend this event. Golf Community Our Golf Community is where LMU students, alumni, lecturers, mentors, corporate partners and supporters hang out together. And you don't even need to play golf to be part of it. The right attitude is a must: You should be open to making new contacts spanning your studies, work and career. You should be willing to actively coordinate and take part in shared community events. ...And for those non-golfers, you should be bold enough to try out at least one golf course. The rest is up to you. If you would like to become part of the LMU Golf Community, apply for membership by reaching out to us via our social media group on LinkedIn . Be sure to tell us about your connection to LMU Munich and why you want to join us. LMU Golf Community membership is free of charge. Participation in our joint networking events, workshops, golf rounds, golf courses or community excursions may incur some personal costs. Regarding additional charges for events, you can expect to be informed in advance via email so that you can then decide whether or not you wish to participate. We are looking forward to hearing from you! Are you an employer and would like to take part in our events? Dirk Erfurth LMU's Career Services Head of Career Service / Business Coach Advanced Send an email More Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/our-services-for-employers/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Our services for employers - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Our services for employers LMU career fairs & recruiting for employers As the central Career Services of LMU, we offer customized career events and services for more than 50,000 students from all faculties and companies from all sectors. Skip to content Talents Meet Companies Basic: Advertise on the LMU job portal Join the virtual LMU Career Fair! Premium services: Many do fairs. We design events! Overview of premium services Costs & Services LMU Career Event or classic fair? A comparison. Event dates for 2026 Event checklists FAQs for companies Guidelines of the LMU Career Services Your contact for all of LMU's Career Events & Fairs Show more Talents Meet Companies If you click to view this video your personal data will be transmitted to YouTube and cookies may also be stored on your device. LMU has no influence over how any such data is transmitted or indeed over its further usage. More information available here: LMU data protection policy , data protection policy from YouTube / Google I acknowledge that I have read and understood the information concerning the protection of my data and am willing to display the embedded content despite potential risks. This short film gives you exclusive insights into our career events. Find out directly from partner companies and students how they experience the events, what opportunities arise from them – and why it benefits you as an employer to be there. 5:12\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t | \n\t\t\t\t\t        \t10 Apr 2025\n\t\t\t\t        \t\t |  \n\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t©LMU Career Service Basic: Advertise on the LMU job portal Post your jobs here Read more You can publish your advertisements for part-time jobs, student traineeships, internships and permanent positions online on our job portal . This allows you to reach students from all subject areas and in all phases of their studies. We offer two options for the duration of publication, tailored to your recruiting needs. We guarantee you visibility and a high reach: The job portal is known to all students in Munich and is highly frequented (more than 1,000 visits/day). Quick guide job exchange In case of problems/questions: There is a support button in the portal. Here you can activate your account for seven days and we can help you quickly and directly. Internships Part-time jobs Working student positions Job advertisements Single advertisements for 4 weeks 90,- 180,- 180,- 240,- Long-term advertisements for 6 months 360,- 540,- 540,- 540,- All prices are listed in euros. Prices are net plus VAT. Please read our general terms & conditions - Discounts or contingent bookings are not possible. We reserve the right to charge a processing fee of 10 euros for any subsequent changes to the invoice details. As an alternative to bank transfer, you are welcome to use our ePayBayern system for payment. There you can pay by credit card, debit card, or PayPal. Please note that due to the high level of effort involved and in view of our modest invoice amounts, we only complete supplier forms for our premium partners. Many forms are designed for B2B contacts and companies that do not apply to us as a public corporation. You will find all the relevant information you need in the LMU Munich legal notice and on the website of the Free State of Bavaria . Team Job-Portal LMU's Career Services Office / Job portal Send an email More Join the virtual LMU Career Fair! Reach more than 50,000 of LMU’s top talents exclusively! Promote your career opportunities and events at two prominent locations. Virtual Career Fair Career & Networking Events 1 year for only EUR 2,995 (net). Secure your spot now and attract top talent for your events and your company. If you’re interested, please contact us. Premium services: Many do fairs. We design events! Book now Read more As LMU’s official Career Service , we have strong ties with all of LMU’s faculties. We are the only place where you can reach all of LMU’s more than 50,000 students in a way that precisely aligns with your defined recruiting goals. In addition to LMU students , students from other public universities and colleges are always welcome to attend our events. Students who take advantage of our events and services are among the most dedicated and successful at LMU. Our career network has grown steadily since 2012. Over 80 percent of the companies have been our clients for more than five years. They value the more intensive and lasting career connections fostered by our programs. In addition, the number of companies joining the network on the recommendation of our graduates increases every year. In 2024, 15 recommendations led to partnerships. We are committed to fostering sustainable and tailored career connections , always keeping the interests of both our students and our corporate partners equally in mind. Attendees at our career fairs consistently report that the interactions at our events are more meaningful and long-lasting , and more often lead to concrete hiring successes . Our events are always held in a pleasant atmosphere with appealing catering for both students and company representatives. Lasting professional connections within an excellent network Our career events and fairs are part of a premium partnership with LMU , as our goal is to foster lasting and tailored connections between students, graduates, and your company or organization. Join the extensive LMU career network and meet the students who match your recruitment profile. Overview of premium services Your advantages at a glance Please refer to the table below for the terms of the partnership. At our exclusive career events , you can get to know students personally and sustainably. We address the students according to your recruiting goals: Studienfach/fächer Phase des Studiums angestrebter Abschluss At all events, you will receive the CVs of the participants in advance so that you can conduct individual interviews with particularly interesting candidates on site and to keep in touch after the events. We also advertise your in-house events for you via our event calendar and in our monthly newsletter to all students. [ Registration form] You can post up to 10 job advertisements per semester free of charge on our job board . You have access to the LMU Talent Pool profiles. You can contact the candidates you are interested in directly at any time. For the duration of your membership, we offer you a virtual exhibition stand on our partner site and invite you to our cultural and sporting events with LMU alumni and students, e.g. the LMU Golf Community . Depending on the package booked, the partnership includes one or more free career treks to your company. As a partner, you can take part in new piloted trade fair formats free of charge . If you wish, you can organize business case workshops with a professionally selected group of students as part of the Q4 Internship Flash . Furthermore, our social media team will visit you on request to shoot an Insta story with you for your and our site. We also regularly report on our partner companies on LinkedIn . We also proactively connect you with students who match your advertised positions. Please book the events via our Career Community Portal . The contract is concluded after we have checked and confirmed the booking. Real Career Networking, Beyond Sharing Give Aways! At LMU Career Service events, you don't (just) impress our students with giveaways and a large exhibition stand. The focus is on your company, your representatives on site, your vision, your mission - in short, your employer brand. Our event participants - companies and students - often tell us afterwards that the career discussions at our events are more intensive, more concrete and more goal-oriented. The students are well prepared, inform themselves in advance about the participating companies and often approach recruiters and experts with concrete application plans . Our events are designed so that all companies have the same exhibition space available for tables, chairs, roll-ups and giveaways. We deliberately do not differentiate according to industry and company size . We provide tables, chairs, electricity, catering and co. Ideally, you come with two roll-ups, at least two representatives and, depending on the size of the event, giveaways for the students in attendance. Our advertising is impressive! With our regularly published flyers, posters and banners at the main building and at the main canteen, we advertise you and your events at LMU all year round at all LMU locations and at the \"Universität\" subway station. Costs & Services model Duration / Number of Career Events Total net price in EUR Premium #1 1 career event 1 Career Trek to your company Premium services for 6 months / 1 semester* 4,500 Premium #2 2 career events 1 free Career Trek Premium services for 12 months / 2 semesters* 25 job advertisements free of charge 6,000 Premium #3 Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 25 job advertisements free of charge 7,500 Booking Single Event 1 Career Event Participation with up to 3 company representatives 2,995 First and second extension of the partnership for existing customers Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Free participation in the Q4 Internship Flash Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 6,000 from the third consecutive renewal of the partnership Up to 4 career events 2 free Career Treks Free participation in the Q4 Internship Flash Premium services for 18 months / 3 semesters* 4,750 * In addition to participating in the event, you will have access to all other Career Service services mentioned above (e.g., talent pool, digital exhibition booth, promotion of your events, etc.) free of charge during the event period. LMU Career Event or classic fair? A comparison. What makes the LMU Career Service events so special? What advantages do they offer compared to regular career fairs? We have summarized the most important points for you. For comparison (PDF, 174 KB) As a partner company, please select your events here . Alternatively, feel free to contact us by email to make your event reservations. Event dates for 2026 Date Format March 27 LMU Shape Your Career! Consulting + STEM – our industry-specific career fair, attracting up to 300 students. Opportunity to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request. May 22 LMU Career Forum – our traditional career fair, attracting up to 300 students; option to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request July 10 LMU Career Talk – our career fair featuring a panel discussion in the morning and a fair in the afternoon, with up to 300 students in attendance ; opportunity to host a keynote speech or workshop upon request October 23 LMU Career Marathon – our fair focused on diversity and inclusion, offering up to 300 students the opportunity to attend a keynote speech or workshop upon request November 13 International Career Event \" Working Here & Abroad \" – our career fair for all students with an international background and/or international career plans. Opportunity to attend a keynote speech or workshop upon request Ongoing and by appointment Every Tuesday at the Literaturhaus or Kardinal Wendel Haus Meet & Greet – As a company, you’ll visit us and meet students who match your recruitment profile. You’ll deliver a keynote speech and present your career opportunities. Ongoing and by appointment Career Trek - We’ll bring a group of up to 25 students who are a good fit for your company to your location. You’ll present your career opportunities on-site and show students and recent graduates their future workplace. Ongoing and by appointment Every Friday online or at Hansa Haus Munich AI Academy for students. If you’re interested in an exciting topic related to the use of AI, then this program is perfect for you. Ongoing and by appointment Every Friday online or at Hansa Haus Munich Q4 Internship: Flash / Business Cases Event checklists FAQs for companies LMU Career Forum - 22.05.2026 The venue is the Kardinal Wendel Haus in Munich , near Münchner Freiheit. The event opens for students at 10:00 a.m. We will be on site for you starting around 9:00 a.m. Please set up your booths between 9:00 and 10:00 a.m. Please have your promotional materials delivered the day before the event and picked up again at the end of the day (5:00 PM – 6:00 PM). Please make sure to label your materials clearly! Catering Schedule Starting at 9:00 AM Welcome coffee and pretzels for company representatives Starting at 10:00 AM Check-in opens and welcome coffee for students 12:00 PM – 1:30 PM Networking buffet for company representatives and students 2:30 PM Coffee and pastries 4:00 PM End of the event You will need one to two roll-up banners and giveaways for approximately 200 students. Students participate on a “hop-on-hop-off” basis. This means that, as expected, there will be a steady flow of visitors throughout the day. Ideally, you should have 2–3 colleagues on site. An exhibition booth is not required. We will provide you with two tables where you can interact with interested students and display promotional materials. Wi-Fi and electricity are available on-site (for your company’s booth; no password required) The dress code for students is open / casual / smart / business casual Students will wear name tags . We generally recommend traveling by public transportation (Münchner Freiheit subway station). Unfortunately, following a decision by the LHST, we cannot provide you with parking passes. There are three parking garages in the immediate vicinity available to you. The event will be documented by our photographer , Sabine Jakobs. Feel free to ask her if she can take a photo of you and your team on-site. Regardless of this, we will try to ensure that every company is featured in one or more photos. We will prepare name tags and LinkedIn profiles for you. Please send us the names, job titles, and LinkedIn links of all participants by 15.05. at the latest ! Shape Your Career! Consulting & MINT am 27.03.2026 Shape Your Career! Consulting & MINT Veranstaltungsort der Messe ist das Literaturhaus München , 3.OG Die Veranstaltung wird um 10:00 Uhr für die Studierenden eröffnet. Wir sind ab 9:00 Uhr für Sie vor Ort. Sie können Rollups / Werbematerial am Vorabend anliefern lassen. Idealerweise aber bringen Sie diese am selben Tag mit und nehmen diese am Abend wieder mit. Bitte achten Sie unbedingt auf ausreichende Beschriftung. Sie benötigen ein bis zwei Rollups und Give Aways für ca. 150 Studierende. Ein Messestand wird nicht benötigt. Sie erhalten einen Tisch von uns, an dem Sie sich mit Interessent/-innen austauschen können und an dem Sie Werbematerial auslegen können. Es gibt vor Ort WiFi und Strom (für Ihren Unternehmensstand). Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist open / casual / smart casual. Die Studierenden tragen Namensschilder. Sie erhalten am Montag vor dem Event die Liste der vorangemeldeten Studierenden und deren CVs. Die CVs können Sie bis zu vier Wochen nach dem Event für Recruiting-Zwecke weiter verwenden, wenn Sie im Einzelfall den Recruiting-Prozess fortsetzen natürlich gemäß Ihren eigenen Datenschutzbestimmungen länger. Wir stellen Ihnen Namensschilder zur Verfügung. Bitte senden Sie bis spätestens 5 Werktage vor dem Event per Email, wer aus Ihrem Unternehmen das Event besuchen und begleiten wird , so dass wir die Namensschilder und Tischunterlagen für Sie erstellen können (LinkedIn-Profile zum Vernetzen). Die Veranstaltung wird von unserer Profifotografin Sabine Jakobs dokumentiert. Sie können sie gerne ansprechen, ob Sie ein Foto von Ihnen und Ihrem Team vor Ort macht. Wir versuchen unabhängig davon, dass jedes Unternehmen auf einem oder mehreren Fotos zu sehen ist. Ablaufplan ab 10:00 Check-In für Studierende 10:00 - 16:00 Messe, Einzelgespräche, Networking, Key-Notes 12:00 - 13:30 Networking Buffet ca. 16 Uhr Ende der Veranstaltung Career Trek Veranstaltungsort ist Ihr Unternehmensstandort. Bitte teilen Sie uns rechtzeitig mit, wo wir uns bei Ihnen treffen. Ihnen steht ein Zeitfenster zur freien Gestaltung von 10:00 - 14:00 zur Verfügung, ein Muster-Ablauf wäre 10:00 Uhr Begrüßung (mit Kaffee) 10:15 Präsentation und oder Rundgang durch das Unternehmen 12:30 Business & Networking Lunch 13:30 Verabschiedung Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist open / casual / smart casual Die Gruppengröße wird idR zwischen 10 und 25 Studierenden sein. Sie erhalten einige Tage im Vorfeld die CVs der Besucher:innen. Die CVs können Sie bis zu vier Wochen nach dem Event für Recruiting-Zwecke weiter verwenden, wenn Sie im Einzelfall den Recruiting-Prozess fortsetzen natürlich gemäß Ihren eigenen Datenschutzbestimmungen länger. Es wäre klasse, wen die Studierenden bei Ihnen vor Ort Personen auf senior, junior und intern Level kennenlernen. Meet & Greet Veranstaltungsort ist das Hansa Haus München , Brienner Str. 39. Das Event beginnt um 18:00 und endet um 20:00. Wir sind ab 17:30 für Sie vor Ort. Rechnen Sie mit 20 - 30 Studierenden, deren CVs Sie im Vorfeld von uns erhalten. Idealerweise besteht Ihr Team vor Ort nicht nur aus senior Mitarbeiter:innen sondern gerne auch aus Fresh(wo:)men, Praktikant:innen und/oder Werkstudent:innen. Für die Unternehmensvorstellung mit anschließender Fragerunde empfehlen wir die erste Stunde. Seien Sie bei dieser möglichst konkret und geben direkte Einblicke in Ihre Arbeit und in Ihren Recruitingprozess. Als Werbematerial reichen zwei Rollups und einige Give Aways aus. Präsentationstechnik ist vor Ort vorhanden. In der zweiten Stunde laden wir Sie und die Studierenden zu einem kleinen Networking Snack ein. Es gibt keinen festen Dresscode. Wir schließen das Event um 20:00 Uhr. Sie können dann das Networking noch bis ca. 20:30 ausklingen lassen. Q4 Internship Flash 2025 - Abschluss-Event am 05.12.2025 Zunächst einmal vielen Dank für all die spannenden Cases im Laufe des Jahres. Wir freuen uns sehr auf das große Abschluss-Messe mit Ihnen allen im Kardinal-Wendel-Haus. Wann: FR 05.12.2025 von 10 - 16 Uhr Eingeladen sind neben den Studierenden, die an den Cases teilgenommen haben, auch andere interessierte Studierende. Diese wollen wir gemeinsam mit Ihnen für das Event kommendes Jahr gewinnen. Ich würde mich sehr freuen, wenn Sie wieder dabei sind in 2026. Das Format der übers Jahr verteilten Cases hat sich bewährt. Bitte füllen Sie zur Teilnahme diesen Bogen aus. Nachfolgend finden Sie die FAQs zur Abschlussmesse. Ort: Kardinal-Wendel-Haus, Mandlstr. 23, München. Wir empfehlen die Anreise mit öffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln. Leider gibt es keine Parkausweise der LHST München mehr. Messematerial: Dieses können Sie am Vorabend ans Veranstaltungshaus senden: Kardinal-Wendel-Haus, Mandlstr. 23, 80802 München, für Messe LMU, zHd. Frau Grünwald. Bitte lassen Sie das Material am Abend des Events wieder abholen (17:00 - 20:00 Uhr). Bei den Giveaways: Rechnen Sie mit 100 - 250 Studierenden, die über den Tag verteilt die Messe besuchen. Sie erhalten wie immer die CVs am Montag vor der Messe. Wir empfehlen unbedingt, die Studierenden persönlich anzuschreiben, deren Profil besonders spannend für Sie ist. z.B.: \"Hallo, schön, dass Du zum Q4 Abschluss Event kommst. Dein Profil könnte zu uns passen. Besuch uns doch an unserem Stand. Wir freuen uns auf Dich.\" - Das erhöht die Verbindlichkeit bei diesem für Studierende kostenfreien Event signifikant. Wir freuen uns sehr auf das Event mit Ihnen. Bei Fragen schreiben Sie uns gerne oder stellen uns einen Calendly / Zoom Termin ein. International Event Working here & abroad - 24.10.2025 Veranstaltungsort: Literaturhaus München, 3. OG ( Salvatorplatz 1, 80333 München ) Die Vormittags-Veranstaltung (zwei Bewerbungs-Workshops) wird um 09:00 Uhr eröffnet. Wir sind ab 08:30 vor Ort. Sie können ab 11:00 für den Messeteil anreisen. Ab 11:30 Uhr gibt es einen Business-Lunch , zu dem Sie herzlich eingeladen sind. Die Messe beginnt um 12:00 Uhr. Sie können Rollups / Werbematerial am Vorabend anliefern lassen (Adresse siehe oben, Ansprechpartnerin vor Ort ist Carolin Frohnauer). Kalkulieren Sie bei Ihrem Werbematerial mit ca. 150 - 200 Studierenden. Ein Messestand wird nicht benötigt. Wir stellen Ihnen Tische und Stühle zur Verfügung. Hier können Sie sich mit Interessentinnen und Interessenten austauschen und Ihr Werbematerial auslegen. Bringen Sie gern bis zu zwei Roll-Ups mit. Der Dresscode der Studierenden ist casual / smart casual. Die Studierenden tragen Namensschilder . Wir werden auch für Sie Namensschilder erstellen. Ebenso bekommen Sie als Unternehmen eine Karte , auf der sich Codes zu Ihren LinkedIn-Profilen befinden, sodass sich Studierende möglichst einfach mit Ihnen verknüpfen können. Legen Sie diese am besten auf Ihrem Tisch aus. Wir empfehlen, mit etwa drei Unternehmensvertreterinnen anzureisen. Hier ist eine Mischung aus HR-Mitarbeitenden sowie Mitarbeitenden aus den Fachbereichen ideal. Wir empfehlen die Anreise mit öffentlichen Verkehrsmitteln . Der Odeonsplatz ist fußläufig 5 Minuten entfernt. Wenige Tage vor dem Event erhalten Sie von uns die Liste mit den Studierenden , die sich für das Event vorangemeldet haben. Sie erhalten zudem die CVs . Wir erwarten am Veranstaltungstag selbst zudem einige spontane Besucherinnen und Besucher. Die Veranstaltung wird von unserer Fotografin Sabine Jakobs dokumentiert. Sie können sie gerne ansprechen, ob sie ein Foto von Ihnen macht. Wir versuchen unabhängig davon, dass jedes Unternehmen auf einem oder mehreren Fotos zu sehen ist. Ihre To-Do's: Bitte teilen Sie uns bis spätestens 19.10 mit, wer aus Ihrem Unternehmen an der Messe teilnehmen wird. Wir benötigen folgende Informationen: Name, Vorname, Positionsbezeichnung, ggf. LinkedIn-Kontakt Bitte teilen Sie uns baldmöglichst mit, welche Studierenden Sie ansprechen möchten ( Studiengang / Fachbereich ). Bewerbung Ihrer eigenen Events Hier können Sie Ihre eigenen Events bewerben. Guidelines of the LMU Career Services Empowerment and Potential Development The focus of our daily work lies in supporting our students in the best possible way on their path toward professional life. We deliberately adopt a strengths-oriented approach and foster the individual potential of our students. Through our broad range of services, we aim to empower students to explore the wide variety of career opportunities, to find their own path in the professional world, and to gain a deeper understanding of themselves and their aspirations. Promotion of Innovation In order to provide optimal support to our students and partners, we regularly integrate current formats, discussions, and impulses into our services. Innovation, openness, and creativity - combined with an awareness of the needs of our target groups - enable us to provide contemporary Career Services, both in person and digitally. Promotion of Diversity As a university with a wide range of disciplines, we experience the added value of interdisciplinary exchange every day. Therefore, our events are generally open to all fields of study. For our partners, interests, skills, and the recruitment of successful new employees do not end at disciplinary boundaries. In addition, we promote our career events in close coordination with our partners and inform students about the primary target groups. Beyond disciplinary diversity, our work is also shaped by the diversity of our students. It is particularly important to us to make our services equally accessible to all LMU Munich students and to promote equal opportunities. The internationalization of universities is an integral part of our services. International students at LMU are a natural part of all our events. Furthermore, through the scholarship programs we administer, we support students in undertaking international internships around the world. Partnership and Exchange Our work is based on a relationship of mutual respect with our students and partners. Mutual trust, transparency, and openness to the unique conditions of the university environment are essential. In addition, we actively promote direct exchange between our various target groups. Your contact for all of LMU's Career Events & Fairs Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Please read our terms & conditions . up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/privacy-policy-career-events-services/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Privacy policy career events & services - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Privacy policy career events & services Privacy Policy The data protection regulations of LMU Munich apply. The following also applies: Data protection information in accordance with Art. 13 GDPR for the use of the \"matorixmatch\" portal application of the LMU Munich Career Service The following data protection information applies to all users of the matorixmatch application of the Career Service of the University of Munich (LMU), hereinafter abbreviated to \"portal application\". It applies to all registered users of the portal application and users of visitor access. When you use the portal application, personal data is collected and processed from and about you. This data is linked to your person. It is therefore our duty to inform you about what data is collected and processed and what rights you have with regard to data collection and processing. 1. responsible body Ludwig Maximilian University Munich Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 80539 Munich Data processing department: LMU Career Service e-mail 2. data protection officer Data Protection Officer of the LMU Munich 3. purpose - What is \"Matorixmatch\" and what can it be used for? Matorixmatch is a SaaS application that the LMU Career Service uses to manage its events and services. The Career Service uses the portal application to establish contacts with mentors and companies from the Career Service's career network. The data is shared exclusively with the companies and between the mentors and mentees, who are selected by the students. When used by students / companies / mentors, the data protection regulations of matorixmatch also apply. If you have any questions, please contact the LMU Career Service / the above-mentioned LMU data protection officer directly. 4. categories of personal data processed Personal data about you is processed as part of the portal application. Below we describe which personal data is processed: 4.1 Logging in to the portal application Uploaded photo Title Gender First names Name Telephone e-mail Preferred display language Uploaded resume Events and consulting services booked and attended by you Your concerns in the consultation Attendance lists The data is uploaded by you and can be entered, edited and deleted at any time. After deletion, only the data that is required from a commercial point of view and with regard to the management of events is stored. 4.2 Cookies We only use consent-free cookies that are used solely for the operation of the platform and do not require separate approval. 5. legal basis The legal basis for the collection and processing of personal data is your consent in accordance with Article 6(1)(a) GDPR. Data processing is carried out in accordance with the relevant data protection regulations, in particular on the basis of the General Data Protection Regulation and the Bavarian Data Protection Act. With regard to the use of cookies, the legal basis is Art. 25 TTDSG. Data processing is also carried out to the extent necessary for the purpose of continuous improvement of system operation, i.e. for quality assurance, by the operator of the portal application (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. e GDPR). 6th recipient We use a suitable IT security infrastructure to ensure that internally only those persons who require access to this information for the fulfillment of their tasks have access to it. We treat personal data confidentially and do not make it available to third parties, especially not to the public, without authorization. 6.1 Internal receivers The data collected will be processed for the purpose described in section 1 by the respective LMU employees and cooperating companies as part of the events and services offered. The employees of the LMU Career Service and companies that you select yourself as part of the events and services have access to the respective data. 6.2 External receivers We only pass on your data to the associated companies, mentors and/or trainers as part of the events and services you have selected. We oblige the companies to comply with the legal requirements on data protection and the usual storage, processing and deletion periods in recruiting. Companies that use student data from the portal are obliged to use the data and documents of students and graduates transmitted to them only for recruiting purposes in the temporal and organizational context of the events booked and used by them and to delete these data and documents no later than four weeks after the event or when the partnership expires. Any longer data processing requires the separate consent of the student or graduate, e.g. as part of the continuation of the application and recruitment process in the respective company. 7. deletion Personal data is deleted from the system as soon as it is no longer required for the purpose for which it was collected. A deletion check is carried out regularly and at least once a year. We block access to participant data immediately after the end of an event. Of course, we will also pass on your deletion request to any companies you have chosen. You can change your data at any time. 8. a) Your rights You have various claims against the responsible body with regard to the data stored about you. Please note that master data provided by external institutions (e.g. universities of the DFN, vhb) can only be accessed, corrected or deleted by the respective institution. Your rights include Right to information (Art. 15 GDPR): You have the right to receive information about the personal data that is processed about you, please note that you can also find the data in your user profile. Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR): If incorrect personal data is stored, you can adjust some of it yourself (profile data you have entered yourself) or request the controller(s) to do so. The controller will comply with the request if the correction is justified and permissible. Right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR): You have the right to have personal data deleted that is demonstrably incorrect or for which the controller cannot prove a processing purpose. There is no right to erasure of personal data if the controller is obliged to retain the data for legal reasons or due to official obligations (proof of instruction, proof of quality assurance, copyright usage rights, examination rights). The obligation to delete personal data may also exist after the end of the course / participation in the course / employment relationship or if consent is withdrawn. There is also no entitlement to deletion if information has been collected by you and this is in an indissoluble context with information from other users (e.g. forum posts). The request for deletion can be interpreted as a withdrawal of consent. This may mean that you will no longer have access to the portal application and participation in a course will no longer be possible. It may no longer be possible to provide evidence, e.g. proof of performance. Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR): Those responsible will ensure that, in the event of a justified restriction of processing, personal data is only accessible to those persons who need to process the data. They may use pseudonymization and anonymization for this purpose. Restricting processing may mean that you will no longer have access to the portal application and participation in a course will no longer be possible. It may no longer be possible to provide evidence, e.g. proof of performance. Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR): You can object to the further use of the data under the legal requirements. This can only take effect in the future. The right to object is not an automatic obligation for the controller to erase the data. If the controller has storage obligations for other legal reasons, these take precedence. The objection may mean that you no longer have access to the portal application and participation in a course is no longer possible. Evidence, e.g. proof of performance, may no longer be able to be provided. Right to data portability Art. 20 GDPR): Under the legal requirements, you have the right to receive data that you have collected yourself in an electronic format that can be used elsewhere. The right is limited to data that is not subject to a business secret and therefore may not be transferred to other parties or that affects the rights of others, e.g. their personal rights or copyright. Right of revocation (Art. 7 para. 3 GDPR): You have the right to withdraw your consent to the processing of your data for the future. The revocation does not affect the legality of the processing up to the time of revocation. Withdrawal may mean that you no longer have access to the portal application and participation in a course is no longer possible. It may no longer be possible to provide evidence, e.g. proof of performance. In the event of a breach of statutory provisions for the protection of the data stored about you, you can contact the competent supervisory authority. The competent supervisory authority is the Bavarian State Commissioner for Data Protection (see § 4). Please contact the controller(s) or the data protection officer(s) first (see § 4) so that your request can be examined as quickly as possible and, if necessary, complied with. In the event of deletion, restriction or revocation, further use of the portal application and access to the learning content stored there as well as participation in the activities and functions available there is no longer guaranteed with immediate effect. 8. b) Recordings, reporting and advertising: Please note that the event will be photographed / filmed and the image material may be published on the Internet or in one of our publications in the context of LMU Career Services. Your personal data will be processed on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 sentence 1 lit. f GDPR. We would like to point out that you can object to this processing in accordance with Art. 21 para. 1 GDPR for reasons arising from your particular situation. We will then no longer process your personal data unless we can demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds for the processing which override your interests, rights and freedoms or the processing serves the establishment, exercise or defense of legal claims. The objection should be addressed to: careerservice@lmu.de, Career Service der LMU, Ludwigstr. 27, 80539 Munich. Of course, you can also object to being photographed on site at any time. Please speak to the photographer/documentarian on site. Examples of publications by LMU / corporate partners: Reports on the Internet / Intranet about an event Reports in social media about an event Advertising future events in a flyer, on the Internet or on social media 9. newsletter and reminder By registering in the Career Community on the matorixmatch portal, you agree that we will inform you regularly by e-mail about events. We will also send you reminders about the dates you have booked. 10. validity The current version of the data protection information applies. If necessary, the data protection information will be adapted. Further data protection information can be found at www.lmu.de/datenschutzerklaerung. 11 Consent under data protection law I have taken note of the data protection information. I am aware that mandatory personal data is processed when using the portal application and that consent is voluntary. I am aware that I will not be given access to the portal application if I do not consent or revoke my consent. I consent to the processing of the data stored in my \"personal profile\" and the contributions published by me in my name. I consent to the processing of the data generated by my use of a \"course\" or the platform. I can view and change this consent at any time on the start page of the portal application. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/user-support-for-our-portal/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "User-Support for our portal - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: User-Support for our portal User help for our career portal Here you will find quick help if you get stuck in our portal (matorix). Skip to content Link our portal with your LMU user ID And if all else fails... In advance: the most common solution to problems Meaning of Step 1 and Step 2 Missing documents Participation dates missing Mobile view \"squeezed\" Format not enabled yet Show more Link our portal with your LMU user ID Enlarge New: You can now link your (already existing) account in the Career Service Portal (matorixmatch) with your LMU user ID for single sign-on (SSO with Shibboleth). If you do not yet have an account, please register first. You will need the data sent to you by e-mail for the one-time/first-time login and you can link your account with the LMU user ID immediately afterwards. And if all else fails... Enlarge If you get stuck with our initial help, simply press the support button in the portal. This will activate your account and we can help you quickly and directly. In advance: the most common solution to problems Enlarge Check whether you have uploaded all the documents required for an offer ( CV, enrollment certificate, job reference ) under Step 1: Career profile Have you activated yourself for the relevant offer under Step 2: Events & Services and, for example, provided all the required additional information (e.g. motivation) for the personal counseling offers ( mentoring, career coaching, application counseling ) before you selected dates? Please login to matorix before using the internal links in these articles. Meaning of Step 1 and Step 2 Enlarge Step 1: Career Profile Here you enter your master data and upload your personal documents. Most error messages have to do with something being missing here. Most of the time it is documents. The safest way is to upload the following right at the beginning: CV German and/or English Certificate of enrollment \"Arbeitszeugnis\" (reference - if you want the reference check) Link to step 1 Step 2: Events & Services Here you can activate your account for all our offers. Before you can re-/deregister (concrete) dates , click on enable format . Please distinguish: Under re-/deregistraion of (concrete) dates you edit individual dates (e.g. individual Meet&Greet) for the selected event or service format. With Deregister of format (completely) you deregister from the entire offer (e.g. all Meet&Greet). Link to step 2 My calendar In the calendar you can see your already booked appointments. If you scroll down, you will also see a calendar view that allows you to select or deselect appointments. You can only book appointments for which you have previously activated the event/service format and for which all required documents have already been uploaded. ( Step 1 and Step 2 ) Missing documents Enlarge Most error messages indicate that documents are missing for the selected format. In the menu, go to Step 1: Career Profile . Scroll down to the Documents item and upload the required ones. e.g.: CV for the CV Check \" Arbeitszeugnis \" / Job reference for the job reference check Certificate of enrollment for the consulting services Participation dates missing Enlarge For the consulting formats career counseling, application counseling and mentoring we need additional information from you. Before choosing a date please first fill out the fields about your motivation / your request. Please (s.above) check als Step 1: Career Profile if you already uploaded all documents necessary. Mobile view \"squeezed\" Enlarge Unfortunately not all browsers load these pages equally well. We are working on this. In this case, we recommend that you rotate your smartphone screen. In the wider display works. Format not enabled yet Enlarge Please Enable format before re-/de-registration of (concrete) dates . You can do this here via Submit. up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    },
    "https://www.lmu.de/en/workspace-for-students/career-services/application-tips-for-students/": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Application tips for students - LMU Munich Navigation und Service Direkt zu: Content Main navigation Search Main navigation Research Study About LMU DE Switch to German / Zur deutschen Sprachversion Open / close search You are in the following website hierarchy: Home Workspace for Students Career Services You are here: Application tips for students Application tips for students Here you will find tips for your application. Skip to content Applications to the German-speaking job market International applications Publications for students We are happy to check your CV! Please register for our CV check . Applications to the German-speaking job market Basic tips for the application documents Submit your documents in one pdf file , unless otherwise requested. Make sure that the file(s) are named in a meaningful, serious and uniform way. Ensure that your documents are clear and uniform . Uniform designs of CV and cover letter look professional and show your eye for detail (e.g. uniformly used color accents). Basic tips for your Curriculum Vitae 1 to a maximum of 2 pages Two-column format Tabular structure A-chronological structure: New information is given first Consistent time specifications , e.g. mm/yyyy - mm/yyyy Consistent indication of activity, institution and location Provide 2-3 bullet points on tasks and activities or additional relevant information under each experience Date and signature at the end of the CV Make sure that the document is a text file, not an image file. Export the document as a pdf file. This information belongs in your CV Heading: \"Curriculum vitae\" or your full name Personal details: Surname, first name, contact details (address, e-mail address, telephone number), optional: pronouns. Make sure you enter a serious and personal e-mail address!, link to your LinkedIn-profile Optional: Application photo . The photo should be professional and appropriate to the position. Choose a monochrome background and avoid selfies or passport photos. Make sure you look friendly and likeable. Academic career Period Degree program Planned degree (e.g. Bachelor of Science, Master of Arts) University (make sure you use the correct spelling!) Place of study Optional: Minor subjects, specializations, projects, thesis titles Practical experience Period Internships, working student positions, part-time jobs, full-time positions, etc. Position title Employer Place of work 2-3 key points each on tasks and activities Voluntary commitment Period Position title Organization Place of work 2-3 key points on tasks and activities Optional Projects (if more than two projects relevant to the position, these can be listed as a separate bullet point) Publications (if relevant for the position, if there are more than five relevant publications, only an excerpt is given) Knowledge and skills: Always indicating the level of knowledge (e.g. basic knowledge, good knowledge) Language skills IT skills Soft skills Optional: Hobbies or interests: Avoid \"standard hobbies\" such as reading and traveling Sample CV Here you can download a sample CV (PDF, 209 KB) . Basic tips for your motivation letter Important: Read the job advertisement carefully. What are the requirements ? What are the tasks and responsibilities ? The motivation letter should not be a retelling of your CV . It should provide real added value. Important: Make the necessary transfer here (reference to your own experience - job) Find out more about the company : On the homepages there are usually the sections “About us”, “News”, or similar. Which values of the company convince you? What are current developments that you like? What do you think makes the institution special? etc. Length : approx. one page Ensure a uniform layout (font, font size) Pay attention to a clear structure Avoid the \"Konjunktiv\" (similar to conditional I and II) Make sure it is easy to understand , even for non-specialists (e.g. in the HR department) Avoid abbreviations and acronyms Avoid describing problems (e.g. with your last employer) Avoid standard motivation letters. Always refer to the company and the specific job advertisement Have your motivation letter proofread : Check the grammar, spelling and formatting This information belongs in your motivation letter Header Own contact details : Address, cell phone number, e-mail address (preferably with real name) Company contact details : full company name with legal form, department (as stated in the advertisement), contact person, address Current date and location (the dates should match the CV) Subject , stating the position title. If available, state the reference number Salutation of the contact person Introduction Spark interest : possibly via an interesting anecdote, current research, a central idea, your values, etc. If you have previously been in contact with the company, the contact person can be mentioned by name Reference can also be made to career fairs , events, etc. if contact has been made here Main part Brief presentation of your own career . Important: no retelling of your CV! The focus should be on the most relevant stages. Make a selection of the experiences that best suit the vacant position. Bundle related subject areas meaningfully. Apply your experience directly to the advertised position and its requirements and tasks. Use concrete examples, projects, research work, etc. that illustrate your expertise and interest. What added value can you provide? This is where the actual transfer from you to the position takes place. Provide evidence of your most important skills , hard skills and soft skills with relevant examples, details and experience Possible questions: Why this job? Why are you a perfect fit for this position? Why this company? Show your motivation and enthusiasm for the company and the position Go into detail about the potential employer ! Why is this exciting for you? Which areas of the corporate culture appeal to you? Which of the company's values are particularly important to you and why? Conclusion Express your anticipation of a job interview If applicable, include notice periods, earliest starting date, salary expectations etc. Add your signature at the end (also possible digitally; no typed repetition of the name under the signature) Sample motivation letter german You can download a sample motivation letter (PDF, 119 KB) here. International applications Basic tips for the application documents In English, a \"Lebenslauf\" is referred to as a “ CV ” or “ curriculum vitae ,” and in the US, it is also called a “ resume .” Submit your documents in a PDF file , unless otherwise requested. Make sure to use meaningful, professional, and consistent file names . Ensure that your documents are clear and consistent . Consistent designs for your resume and cover letter look professional and show your attention to detail (e.g., consistent use of color accents). Choice of language: We advise you to apply in English for English-language job advertisements and in German for German-language job advertisements. This information belongs in your english CV Heading : “Curriculum Vitae” or your full name Personal details: Last name, first name, contact details (address, email address, phone number), optional: pronouns. Be sure to provide a professional and personal email address! For legal reasons, the following information should NOT be included in your CV: gender, date of birth, marital status, religion, nationality. Also, NO photo. Personal profile / Summary Approximately 2 to 4 sentences A short section about yourself. Briefly summarize your experience and knowledge in a way that is specific to the position. Example: Enthusiastic business student with internship experience in marketing and project management. Strong communication and analytical skills, eager to contribute to a fast-paced international team environment. Academic background (education) Period Course of study Planned degree (e.g., Bachelor of Science, Master of Arts) University (please ensure the spelling is correct!) Place of study (city, country) Optional: Minor subjects, specializations, projects, titles of theses For German degrees/grades, it may be useful to convert them to the 4.0 system Example: GPA: 1.5 (converted to 3.8/4.0 scale) Work experience Period Internships, working student positions, part-time jobs, full-time positions, etc. Job title Employer Place of work 2-3 bullet points each on tasks and activities Tip: Quantify your achievements! Numbers make successes tangible. Examples: “Increased social media engagement by 40%” / “Managed a budget of $5,000” Knowledge and skills: Always indicate your level of knowledge (e.g., basic knowledge, good knowledge) Language skills (CEFR level) IT skills Soft skills Volunteering or projects Period Position title Organization Place of work 2-3 key points about tasks and activities Certificates / Awards / Publications / References (optional) if relevant stating the year Sample CV Here you can download a sample CV (PDF, 97 KB) . Publications for students Students at LMU Munich can download all books from our Kompass series—covering topics related to studying and careers—free of charge via the following permalinks. Der Kompass zum perfekten Praktikum Kompass Digitale Bewerbung : für Student*innen und Absolvent*innen Der Karriere-Kompass für Studierende : ein Arbeitsbuch zur Selbstreflexion und Orientierung Der Kompass zum digitalen Mentoring & Coaching : digitale Beratung entwerfen, gestalten und durchführen Der Mentoring Kompass für Unternehmen und Mentoren : persönliche Erfahrungsberichte, Erfolgsprinzipien aus Forschung und Praxis Mentoring beim Übergang vom Studium in den Beruf Johanna Uitz, M.A. LMU's Career Services Consultant for Internationalization & Employability / project manager FIT-LMU International Careers, Events & Seminars, Mentoring, Employer Services Send an email More Dr.phil. Stephan Pflaum LMU's Career Services Consultant Career Events & Services / Deputy Head of Career Service Send an email Zoom appointment for employers More up Share To share copy Link Share on Facebook Share on Bluesky Share on LinkedIn Related links Home Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Routing Facebook Bluesky Instagram LinkedIn Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München Geschwister-Scholl-Platz 1 D-80539 München Tel: +49 89 2180-0 Fax: +49 89 2180-2322 Related links Sitemap Privacy policy Imprint Accessibility Press Room LMU Shop LMU München © 2021 What are you looking for? main website all LMU sites More information about Google data transfer in LMU's Privacy Policy. close"
    }
  },
